    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-8-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Functions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-8-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the Australian Federal Police are:\n(a) subject to subsection (1A), the provision of police services in\nrelation to the Australian Capital Territory; and\n(aa) the provision of police services in relation to the Jervis Bay\nTerritory; and\n(b) the provision of police services in relation to:\n\n\nConstitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II\nConstitution, functions and laws conferring powers on members etc.  Division 1\nSection 8\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(i) laws of the Commonwealth;\n(ii) property of the Commonwealth (including\nCommonwealth places) and property of authorities of\nthe Commonwealth; and\n(iii) the safeguarding of Commonwealth interests; and\n(baa) the investigation of State offences that have a federal aspect;\nand\n(ba) the provision of services in accordance with arrangements\nentered into under subsection (1C) and doing anything else\nincluded in the arrangements that is incidental or conducive\nto the provision of the services; and\n(bb) to perform the functions conferred by the Witness Protection\nAct 1994; and\n(bc) to perform the functions conferred by a law of a State or\nTerritory that is a complementary witness protection law for\nthe purposes of the Witness Protection Act 1994; and\n(bd) to perform functions under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002;\nand\n(be) to perform such protective and custodial functions as the\nMinister directs by notice in writing in the Gazette, being\nfunctions that relate to a person, matter or thing with respect\nto which the Parliament has legislative power; and\n(bf) the provision of police services and police support services\nfor the purposes of assisting, or cooperating with, an\nAustralian or foreign:\n(i) law enforcement agency; or\n(ii) intelligence or security agency; or\n(iii) government regulatory agency; and\n(bg) the provision of police services and police support services in\nrelation to establishing, developing and monitoring peace,\nstability and security in foreign countries; and\n(bh) to assist or cooperate with:\n(i) an international organisation; or\n(ii) a non-governmental organisation, in relation to acts,\nomissions, matters or things outside Australia;",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The functions of the Australian Federal Police are:\n(a) subject to subsection (1A), the provision of police services in\nrelation to the Australian Capital Territory; and\n(aa) the provision of police services in relation to the Jervis Bay\nTerritory; and\n(b) the provision of police services in relation to:\n\n\nConstitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II\nConstitution, functions and laws conferring powers on members etc.  Division 1\nSection 8\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(i) laws of the Commonwealth;\n(ii) property of the Commonwealth (including\nCommonwealth places) and property of authorities of\nthe Commonwealth; and\n(iii) the safeguarding of Commonwealth interests; and\n(baa) the investigation of State offences that have a federal aspect;\nand\n(ba) the provision of services in accordance with arrangements\nentered into under subsection (1C) and doing anything else\nincluded in the arrangements that is incidental or conducive\nto the provision of the services; and\n(bb) to perform the functions conferred by the Witness Protection\nAct 1994; and\n(bc) to perform the functions conferred by a law of a State or\nTerritory that is a complementary witness protection law for\nthe purposes of the Witness Protection Act 1994; and\n(bd) to perform functions under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002;\nand\n(be) to perform such protective and custodial functions as the\nMinister directs by notice in writing in the Gazette, being\nfunctions that relate to a person, matter or thing with respect\nto which the Parliament has legislative power; and\n(bf) the provision of police services and police support services\nfor the purposes of assisting, or cooperating with, an\nAustralian or foreign:\n(i) law enforcement agency; or\n(ii) intelligence or security agency; or\n(iii) government regulatory agency; and\n(bg) the provision of police services and police support services in\nrelation to establishing, developing and monitoring peace,\nstability and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-8-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-8-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-8-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-8-2-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-8-2-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-8-2-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "caeff11367e90e4a3ddeb1cfa49ef8b75d53bf33db51ee6c55781c4ffbe13215",
      "skos:note": "Provision of police services in relation to various matters"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-8-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Functions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the Australian Federal Police are:\n(a) subject to subsection (1A), the provision of police services in\nrelation to the Australian Capital Territory; and\n(aa) the provision of police services in relation to the Jervis Bay\nTerritory; and\n(b) the provision of police services in relation to:\n\n\nConstitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II\nConstitution, functions and laws conferring powers on members etc.  Division 1\nSection 8\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(i) laws of the Commonwealth;\n(ii) property of the Commonwealth (including\nCommonwealth places) and property of authorities of\nthe Commonwealth; and\n(iii) the safeguarding of Commonwealth interests; and\n(baa) the investigation of State offences that have a federal aspect;\nand\n(ba) the provision of services in accordance with arrangements\nentered into under subsection (1C) and doing anything else\nincluded in the arrangements that is incidental or conducive\nto the provision of the services; and\n(bb) to perform the functions conferred by the Witness Protection\nAct 1994; and\n(bc) to perform the functions conferred by a law of a State or\nTerritory that is a complementary witness protection law for\nthe purposes of the Witness Protection Act 1994; and\n(bd) to perform functions under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002;\nand\n(be) to perform such protective and custodial functions as the\nMinister directs by notice in writing in the Gazette, being\nfunctions that relate to a person, matter or thing with respect\nto which the Parliament has legislative power; and\n(bf) the provision of police services and police support services\nfor the purposes of assisting, or cooperating with, an\nAustralian or foreign:\n(i) law enforcement agency; or\n(ii) intelligence or security agency; or\n(iii) government regulatory agency; and\n(bg) the provision of police services and police support services in\nrelation to establishing, developing and monitoring peace,\nstability and security in foreign countries; and\n(bh) to assist or cooperate with:\n(i) an international organisation; or\n(ii) a non-governmental organisation, in relation to acts,\nomissions, matters or things outside Australia;"
    },
    {
