      },
      "cml:operator": "Justification",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Justification for the prohibition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Protective service officer must not cause death or grievous bodily harm unless necessary to protect life or prevent serious injury.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The justification is that the protective service officer has a duty to protect life and prevent serious injury."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14C Arrested person to be informed of grounds of arrest",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-14c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence\nmust inform the person, at the time of the arrest, of the offence for\nwhich the person is arrested.\n(2) It is sufficient compliance with subsection (1) if the protective\nservice officer informs the person of the substance of the offence,\nand it is not necessary to do so in language of a precise or technical\nnature.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the arrest by a protective service\nofficer of a person for an offence if the person, by his or her own\nactions, makes it impracticable for the protective service officer to\ninform the person of the offence.\n(4) Where a protective service officer who arrests a person for an\noffence believes or has reasonable grounds for believing that the\nperson is unable, by reason of inadequate knowledge of the English\nlanguage or any physical or mental disability, to understand the\nsubstance of the offence for which the person is arrested, the\nprotective service officer must, as soon as practicable, take all\nreasonable steps to ensure that the person is provided with an\nexplanation of the substance of the offence that the person is able\nto understand.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence\nmust inform the person, at the time of the arrest, of the offence for\nwhich the person is arrested.\n(2) It is sufficient compliance with subsection (1) if the protective\nservice officer informs the person of the substance of the offence,\nand it is not necessary to do so in language of a precise or technical\nnature.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the arrest by a protective service\nofficer of a person for an offence if the person, by his or her own\nactions, makes it impracticable for the protective service officer to\ninform the person of the offence.\n(4) Where a protective service officer who arrests a person for an\noffence believes or has reasonable grounds for believing that the\nperson is unable, by reason of inadequate knowledge of the English\nlanguage or any physical or mental disability, to understand the\nsubstance of the offence for which the person is arrested, the\nprotective service officer must, as soon as practicable, take all\nreasonable steps to ensure that the person is provided with an\nexplanation of the substance of the offence that the person is able\nto understand.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14c-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14c-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "12c50d01fe41bf7d07dd2a9dc3279857d4dc3cd09df72c74ab76321dd11522b8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-14c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14C Arrested person to be informed of grounds of arrest",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence\nmust inform the person, at the time of the arrest, of the offence for\nwhich the person is arrested.\n(2) It is sufficient compliance with subsection (1) if the protective\nservice officer informs the person of the substance of the offence,\nand it is not necessary to do so in language of a precise or technical\nnature.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the arrest by a protective service\nofficer of a person for an offence if the person, by his or her own\nactions, makes it impracticable for the protective service officer to\ninform the person of the offence.\n(4) Where a protective service officer who arrests a person for an\noffence believes or has reasonable grounds for believing that the\nperson is unable, by reason of inadequate knowledge of the English\nlanguage or any physical or mental disability, to understand the\nsubstance of the offence for which the person is arrested, the\nprotective service officer must, as soon as practicable, take all\nreasonable steps to ensure that the person is provided with an\nexplanation of the substance of the offence that the person is able\nto understand."
    },
