    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14E How arrested person to be dealt with",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-14e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence\nmust ensure that the person is delivered into the custody of a police\nofficer as soon as practicable to be dealt with according to law.\n(2) Where a weapon or other thing has been seized from the person\nunder subsection 14D(5), the protective service officer must ensure\nthat the weapon or other thing is delivered to the police officer into\nwhose custody the person is delivered.\n(3) In this section:\npolice officer means:\n(a) a member or special member; or\n(b) a member, however described, of a police force of a State or\nTerritory; or\n(c) a member, however described, of a police force of a foreign\ncountry.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence\nmust ensure that the person is delivered into the custody of a police\nofficer as soon as practicable to be dealt with according to law.\n(2) Where a weapon or other thing has been seized from the person\nunder subsection 14D(5), the protective service officer must ensure\nthat the weapon or other thing is delivered to the police officer into\nwhose custody the person is delivered.\n(3) In this section:\npolice officer means:\n(a) a member or special member; or\n(b) a member, however described, of a police force of a State or\nTerritory; or\n(c) a member, however described, of a police force of a foreign\ncountry.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14e-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "06924dfa564cbc5c3d0ae0c2ca58784a2575dfe4ed8ddcbb1c8baffb78d1873c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-14e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14E How arrested person to be dealt with",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence\nmust ensure that the person is delivered into the custody of a police\nofficer as soon as practicable to be dealt with according to law.\n(2) Where a weapon or other thing has been seized from the person\nunder subsection 14D(5), the protective service officer must ensure\nthat the weapon or other thing is delivered to the police officer into\nwhose custody the person is delivered.\n(3) In this section:\npolice officer means:\n(a) a member or special member; or\n(b) a member, however described, of a police force of a State or\nTerritory; or\n(c) a member, however described, of a police force of a foreign\ncountry."
    },
