      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subject to subsection (2), the powers conferred, and duties\nimposed, by this Division on protective service officers are in\n\n\nConstitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II\nPowers and duties of protective service officers  Division 3\nSection 14G\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\naddition to, and not in derogation of, any other powers conferred,\nor duties imposed, by any other law of the Commonwealth or the\nlaw of a State or Territory, and this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the operation of any other law of the\nCommonwealth or the law of a State or Territory providing for\nsuch powers or duties in so far as it is capable of operating\nconcurrently with this Division."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14g-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14g-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
