      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Designated person requests personal information from suspect",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Suspect provides requested information as part of the designated person's cognitive action"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14h-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14H(2) Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-14h-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a designated person:\n(a) makes a request under subsection (1); and\n(b) informs the suspect of the designated person’s authority to\nmake the request; and\n(c) informs the suspect that it may be an offence not to comply\nwith the request;\nthe suspect must not:\n(d) fail to comply with the request; or\n(e) give a name or address that is false in a material particular.\nPenalty: 20 penalty units.\nNote:\nA more serious offence of obstructing a Commonwealth public\nofficial may also apply (see section 149.1 of the Criminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If a designated person:\n(a) makes a request under subsection (1); and\n(b) informs the suspect of the designated person’s authority to\nmake the request; and\n(c) informs the suspect that it may be an offence not to comply\nwith the request;\nthe suspect must not:\n(d) fail to comply with the request; or\n(e) give a name or address that is false in a material particular.\nPenalty: 20 penalty units.\nNote:\nA more serious offence of obstructing a Commonwealth public\nofficial may also apply (see section 149.1 of the Criminal Code).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14h-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14h-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "68225f0d13aa8cc7905178f9d543053ef65f8c32234ac1e56741c3cc3c39a2d7",
      "skos:note": "Suspect must comply with request from designated person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-14h-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14H(2) Definitions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a designated person:\n(a) makes a request under subsection (1); and\n(b) informs the suspect of the designated person’s authority to\nmake the request; and\n(c) informs the suspect that it may be an offence not to comply\nwith the request;\nthe suspect must not:\n(d) fail to comply with the request; or\n(e) give a name or address that is false in a material particular.\nPenalty: 20 penalty units.\nNote:\nA more serious offence of obstructing a Commonwealth public\nofficial may also apply (see section 149.1 of the Criminal Code)."
    },
