          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14h-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14h-ss-3-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "db19c1b982837412a7f3d3199457d9cb2294d3679a7f27bdac2ac59362b5a683",
      "skos:note": "Defendant bears evidential burden in relation to reasonable excuse.",
      "dc:description": "Evidence of reasonable excuse"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-14h-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14H(3) Definitions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the suspect has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."
    },
