    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Acting Commissioner and Deputy Commissioner during vacancy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(1) At any time when the office of Commissioner or an office of\nDeputy Commissioner is or is expected to be vacant (whether or\nnot the office has previously been filled), the Minister may appoint\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nCommissioner and Deputy Commissioners  Division 1\nSection 19\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\na person to act as Commissioner or as a Deputy Commissioner, as\nthe case may be, until the filling of the vacancy.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) While a person is acting as Commissioner or as a Deputy\nCommissioner under subsection (1), he or she has, and may\nexercise, all the powers (except a power to make a declaration\nunder subsection 40D(4)), and shall perform all the functions and\nduties, of the Commissioner or of the Deputy Commissioner, as the\ncase may be.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) At any time when the office of Commissioner or an office of\nDeputy Commissioner is or is expected to be vacant (whether or\nnot the office has previously been filled), the Minister may appoint\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nCommissioner and Deputy Commissioners  Division 1\nSection 19\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\na person to act as Commissioner or as a Deputy Commissioner, as\nthe case may be, until the filling of the vacancy.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) While a person is acting as Commissioner or as a Deputy\nCommissioner under subsection (1), he or she has, and may\nexercise, all the powers (except a power to make a declaration\nunder subsection 40D(4)), and shall perform all the functions and\nduties, of the Commissioner or of the Deputy Commissioner, as the\ncase may be.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-18-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-18-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a894027cb8ebcee4d2f379f7a68033863098015878c5d13c2f6e05ba235f7f9a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Acting Commissioner and Deputy Commissioner during vacancy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(1) At any time when the office of Commissioner or an office of\nDeputy Commissioner is or is expected to be vacant (whether or\nnot the office has previously been filled), the Minister may appoint\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nCommissioner and Deputy Commissioners  Division 1\nSection 19\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\na person to act as Commissioner or as a Deputy Commissioner, as\nthe case may be, until the filling of the vacancy.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) While a person is acting as Commissioner or as a Deputy\nCommissioner under subsection (1), he or she has, and may\nexercise, all the powers (except a power to make a declaration\nunder subsection 40D(4)), and shall perform all the functions and\nduties, of the Commissioner or of the Deputy Commissioner, as the\ncase may be."
    },
