          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-18-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6943d036f08c7f011a6ed644c876008d9bc9c1e8a26f674b49fdcff98042aa86",
      "skos:note": "Minister may appoint person to act as Commissioner or Deputy Commissioner during vacancy."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-18-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18(1) Acting Commissioner and Deputy Commissioner during vacancy",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(1) At any time when the office of Commissioner or an office of\nDeputy Commissioner is or is expected to be vacant (whether or\nnot the office has previously been filled), the Minister may appoint\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nCommissioner and Deputy Commissioners  Division 1\nSection 19\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\na person to act as Commissioner or as a Deputy Commissioner, as\nthe case may be, until the filling of the vacancy.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-18-ss-1-norm",
