    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Leave of absence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner has such recreation leave entitlements as are\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal.\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nCommissioner and Deputy Commissioners  Division 1\nSection 22\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(1A) The Minister may grant the Commissioner leave of absence, other\nthan recreation leave, on such terms and conditions as to\nremuneration or otherwise as the Minister determines.\n(2) The Commissioner may grant leave of absence to a Deputy\nCommissioner on such terms and conditions as to remuneration or\notherwise as the Commissioner determines.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner has such recreation leave entitlements as are\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal.\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nCommissioner and Deputy Commissioners  Division 1\nSection 22\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(1A) The Minister may grant the Commissioner leave of absence, other\nthan recreation leave, on such terms and conditions as to\nremuneration or otherwise as the Minister determines.\n(2) The Commissioner may grant leave of absence to a Deputy\nCommissioner on such terms and conditions as to remuneration or\notherwise as the Commissioner determines.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-21-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-21-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-21-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0588ef9dc752ff22992202c4a1fab4ff643c0b56c417585f4a84038c38819d63"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Leave of absence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner has such recreation leave entitlements as are\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal.\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nCommissioner and Deputy Commissioners  Division 1\nSection 22\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(1A) The Minister may grant the Commissioner leave of absence, other\nthan recreation leave, on such terms and conditions as to\nremuneration or otherwise as the Minister determines.\n(2) The Commissioner may grant leave of absence to a Deputy\nCommissioner on such terms and conditions as to remuneration or\notherwise as the Commissioner determines."
    },
    {
