      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before the Commissioner retires an AFP employee under\nsubsection (1), the employee may, by notice in writing given to the\nCommissioner, consent to the Commissioner retiring the employee\nunder that subsection.\nNote:\nTo find out when an AFP employee’s retirement takes effect in such a\ncase, see section 33.\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nAFP employees  Division 2\nSection 32\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nAFP employee not re-engaged because of invalidity",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Before the Commissioner retires an AFP employee under\nsubsection (1), the employee may, by notice in writing given to the\nCommissioner, consent to the Commissioner retiring the employee\nunder that subsection.\nNote:\nTo find out when an AFP employee’s retirement takes effect in such a\ncase, see section 33.\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nAFP employees  Division 2\nSection 32\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nAFP employee not re-engaged because of invalidity",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "efa0c383587e6c9d6d9625caa1b30f4a9ee8ab828b4e40964e4fe37975455adb",
      "skos:note": "Employee may consent to retirement under subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-32-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32(2) Retirement on invalidity grounds",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before the Commissioner retires an AFP employee under\nsubsection (1), the employee may, by notice in writing given to the\nCommissioner, consent to the Commissioner retiring the employee\nunder that subsection.\nNote:\nTo find out when an AFP employee’s retirement takes effect in such a\ncase, see section 33.\n\n\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III\nAFP employees  Division 2\nSection 32\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nAFP employee not re-engaged because of invalidity"
    },
