        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32(3) Retirement on invalidity grounds",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-32-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n(a) a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for\na period; and\n(b) the person completes that period of engagement (the initial\nperiod); and\n(c) the person is not re-engaged under that section for a further\nperiod starting immediately after the end of the initial period;\nand\n(d) the Commissioner certifies in writing that the person’s\nphysical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the\nperson was not so re-engaged;\nthe person is taken, for the purposes of the Safety, Rehabilitation\nand Compensation Act 1988, the Superannuation Act and the\nSuperannuation Act 2005, to have been retired under this section\non the day on which the initial period ended.\nAFP employee is an eligible employee under the Superannuation\nAct 1976",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If:\n(a) a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for\na period; and\n(b) the person completes that period of engagement (the initial\nperiod); and\n(c) the person is not re-engaged under that section for a further\nperiod starting immediately after the end of the initial period;\nand\n(d) the Commissioner certifies in writing that the person’s\nphysical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the\nperson was not so re-engaged;\nthe person is taken, for the purposes of the Safety, Rehabilitation\nand Compensation Act 1988, the Superannuation Act and the\nSuperannuation Act 2005, to have been retired under this section\non the day on which the initial period ended.\nAFP employee is an eligible employee under the Superannuation\nAct 1976",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9af1041f96880129590fd80ee6aa039d87b31ba45c13c9b272dde5e19ee73fc8",
      "skos:note": "Certification of incapacity is required for retirement on invalidity grounds.",
      "dc:description": "Commissioner's certification"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-32-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32(3) Retirement on invalidity grounds",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n(a) a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for\na period; and\n(b) the person completes that period of engagement (the initial\nperiod); and\n(c) the person is not re-engaged under that section for a further\nperiod starting immediately after the end of the initial period;\nand\n(d) the Commissioner certifies in writing that the person’s\nphysical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the\nperson was not so re-engaged;\nthe person is taken, for the purposes of the Safety, Rehabilitation\nand Compensation Act 1988, the Superannuation Act and the\nSuperannuation Act 2005, to have been retired under this section\non the day on which the initial period ended.\nAFP employee is an eligible employee under the Superannuation\nAct 1976"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Certification is required for retirement.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Commissioner certifies in writing that the person's physical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the person was not re-engaged.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is taken to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Certification must be made during the initial period.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) If: a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for a period; and the person completes that period of engagement (the initial period);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is taken to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Certification must be made until the end of the initial period.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) If: a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for a period; and the person completes that period of engagement (the initial period);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is taken to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "must be re-engaged",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Re-engagement is required after the end of the initial period.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the person is not re-engaged under that section for a further period starting immediately after the end of the initial period;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is taken to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is not certified",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Failure to certify incapacity results in non-retirement.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) the Commissioner certifies in writing that the person’s physical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the person was not so re-engaged;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is taken to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32(4) Retirement on invalidity grounds",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-32-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In spite of this section, an AFP employee who:\n(a) is an eligible employee for the purposes of the\nSuperannuation Act 1976; and\n(b) has not reached his or her maximum retiring age (within the\nmeaning of that Act);\nis not capable of being retired on the ground of invalidity (within\nthe meaning of Part IVA of that Act) unless CSC has given a\ncertificate under section 54C of that Act.\nAFP employee is a member of the superannuation scheme under\nthe Superannuation Act 1990",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In spite of this section, an AFP employee who:\n(a) is an eligible employee for the purposes of the\nSuperannuation Act 1976; and\n(b) has not reached his or her maximum retiring age (within the\nmeaning of that Act);\nis not capable of being retired on the ground of invalidity (within\nthe meaning of Part IVA of that Act) unless CSC has given a\ncertificate under section 54C of that Act.\nAFP employee is a member of the superannuation scheme under\nthe Superannuation Act 1990",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "50e79577c18e2482a428bc8793405bba1d16191d0fbfa258b187ad69ca60bdfc",
      "skos:note": "AFP employee must provide CSC certificate for retirement on invalidity grounds",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-32-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32(4) Retirement on invalidity grounds",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In spite of this section, an AFP employee who:\n(a) is an eligible employee for the purposes of the\nSuperannuation Act 1976; and\n(b) has not reached his or her maximum retiring age (within the\nmeaning of that Act);\nis not capable of being retired on the ground of invalidity (within\nthe meaning of Part IVA of that Act) unless CSC has given a\ncertificate under section 54C of that Act.\nAFP employee is a member of the superannuation scheme under\nthe Superannuation Act 1990"
    },
    {
