    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33(4) Time when retirement on invalidity grounds takes effect",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-33-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The regulations may make provision in relation to the review of\ndecisions of the Commissioner to retire AFP employees under\nsubsection 32(1), where the employees have not consented to being\nretired under that subsection, including:\n(a) the period within which, and the manner in which, AFP\nemployees may apply for review of such decisions; and\n(b) the powers available to a person or body conducting such a\nreview; and\n(c) if the regulations make provision for a person or body\nconducting such a review to make recommendations to the\nCommissioner—the Commissioner giving effect to such\nrecommendations by confirming or revoking such decisions.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The regulations may make provision in relation to the review of\ndecisions of the Commissioner to retire AFP employees under\nsubsection 32(1), where the employees have not consented to being\nretired under that subsection, including:\n(a) the period within which, and the manner in which, AFP\nemployees may apply for review of such decisions; and\n(b) the powers available to a person or body conducting such a\nreview; and\n(c) if the regulations make provision for a person or body\nconducting such a review to make recommendations to the\nCommissioner—the Commissioner giving effect to such\nrecommendations by confirming or revoking such decisions.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43298c0427fe6191687f6e63fb17094c91da3cd79ee264e5a57dea530265f4f7",
      "skos:note": "Regulations must provide for review of decisions to retire AFP employees under subsection 32(1) without consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-33-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33(4) Time when retirement on invalidity grounds takes effect",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The regulations may make provision in relation to the review of\ndecisions of the Commissioner to retire AFP employees under\nsubsection 32(1), where the employees have not consented to being\nretired under that subsection, including:\n(a) the period within which, and the manner in which, AFP\nemployees may apply for review of such decisions; and\n(b) the powers available to a person or body conducting such a\nreview; and\n(c) if the regulations make provision for a person or body\nconducting such a review to make recommendations to the\nCommissioner—the Commissioner giving effect to such\nrecommendations by confirming or revoking such decisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulations must provide for review of decisions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33(5) Time when retirement on invalidity grounds takes effect",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-33-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Despite section 25D of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, if\nregulations under subsection (4) make provision for a person or\nbody conducting a review of decisions of a kind mentioned in that\nsubsection to:\n(a) give written reasons for any decision the person or body\nmakes in relation to such a review; and\n(b) give a copy of those reasons to the AFP employee concerned;\nthe regulations may also make provision in relation to:\n(c) the exclusion from that copy of any information of a medical\nor psychiatric nature that the person or body thinks may be\nprejudicial to the employee’s physical or mental health or\nwell-being; and\n(d) the employee nominating a medical practitioner to receive\nthat information.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Despite section 25D of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, if\nregulations under subsection (4) make provision for a person or\nbody conducting a review of decisions of a kind mentioned in that\nsubsection to:\n(a) give written reasons for any decision the person or body\nmakes in relation to such a review; and\n(b) give a copy of those reasons to the AFP employee concerned;\nthe regulations may also make provision in relation to:\n(c) the exclusion from that copy of any information of a medical\nor psychiatric nature that the person or body thinks may be\nprejudicial to the employee’s physical or mental health or\nwell-being; and\n(d) the employee nominating a medical practitioner to receive\nthat information.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bf378c0661bc2a42cf00329edb1e76758e4451f55f17be10e7fd928d2834dcc8",
      "skos:note": "Regulations must provide written reasons for decisions and a copy of those reasons to the AFP employee concerned.",
      "dc:description": "yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-33-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33(5) Time when retirement on invalidity grounds takes effect",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Despite section 25D of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, if\nregulations under subsection (4) make provision for a person or\nbody conducting a review of decisions of a kind mentioned in that\nsubsection to:\n(a) give written reasons for any decision the person or body\nmakes in relation to such a review; and\n(b) give a copy of those reasons to the AFP employee concerned;\nthe regulations may also make provision in relation to:\n(c) the exclusion from that copy of any information of a medical\nor psychiatric nature that the person or body thinks may be\nprejudicial to the employee’s physical or mental health or\nwell-being; and\n(d) the employee nominating a medical practitioner to receive\nthat information."
    },
