    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "37 General administration and control",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-37"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this Act, the Commissioner has the general\nadministration of, and the control of the operations of, the\nAustralian Federal Police.\nMinisterial directions\n(2) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, give written directions to the\nCommissioner with respect to the general policy to be pursued in\nrelation to the performance of the functions of the Australian\nFederal Police.\n(3) In addition to his or her power to give directions under\nsubsection (2), the Minister may give written directions (either\nspecific or general) to the Commissioner in relation to the use of\ncommon services in accordance with an arrangement made under\nsubsection (5).\nCommissioner must comply with directions\n(4) The Commissioner must comply with all directions given under\nthis section.\nMinisterial arrangements\n(5) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, make an arrangement with the\nappropriate Minister of a State for the provision or development of\ncommon services and for the use of such common services by the\nAustralian Federal Police and the Police Force of the State.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this Act, the Commissioner has the general\nadministration of, and the control of the operations of, the\nAustralian Federal Police.\nMinisterial directions\n(2) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, give written directions to the\nCommissioner with respect to the general policy to be pursued in\nrelation to the performance of the functions of the Australian\nFederal Police.\n(3) In addition to his or her power to give directions under\nsubsection (2), the Minister may give written directions (either\nspecific or general) to the Commissioner in relation to the use of\ncommon services in accordance with an arrangement made under\nsubsection (5).\nCommissioner must comply with directions\n(4) The Commissioner must comply with all directions given under\nthis section.\nMinisterial arrangements\n(5) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, make an arrangement with the\nappropriate Minister of a State for the provision or development of\ncommon services and for the use of such common services by the\nAustralian Federal Police and the Police Force of the State.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "154b55dc65ad064d36e5caf23dd61a6c66b565eaa35cb2284db624c10609c55b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-37",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "37 General administration and control",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this Act, the Commissioner has the general\nadministration of, and the control of the operations of, the\nAustralian Federal Police.\nMinisterial directions\n(2) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, give written directions to the\nCommissioner with respect to the general policy to be pursued in\nrelation to the performance of the functions of the Australian\nFederal Police.\n(3) In addition to his or her power to give directions under\nsubsection (2), the Minister may give written directions (either\nspecific or general) to the Commissioner in relation to the use of\ncommon services in accordance with an arrangement made under\nsubsection (5).\nCommissioner must comply with directions\n(4) The Commissioner must comply with all directions given under\nthis section.\nMinisterial arrangements\n(5) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, make an arrangement with the\nappropriate Minister of a State for the provision or development of\ncommon services and for the use of such common services by the\nAustralian Federal Police and the Police Force of the State."
    },
