    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "37(5) General administration and control",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-37-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, make an arrangement with the\nappropriate Minister of a State for the provision or development of\ncommon services and for the use of such common services by the\nAustralian Federal Police and the Police Force of the State.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, make an arrangement with the\nappropriate Minister of a State for the provision or development of\ncommon services and for the use of such common services by the\nAustralian Federal Police and the Police Force of the State.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ecebbd01a600d5a566a367810631ace76bb056d13ff238f1328e1b6f73482dca",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may make an arrangement with a State for the provision or development of common services."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-37-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "37(5) General administration and control",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the\nCommissioner and of the Secretary, make an arrangement with the\nappropriate Minister of a State for the provision or development of\ncommon services and for the use of such common services by the\nAustralian Federal Police and the Police Force of the State."
    },
