    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40 Compliance with specific directions, instructions or orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "An AFP appointee must not:\n(a) disobey; or\n(b) fail to carry out;\na lawful direction, instruction or order, whether written or oral,\ngiven to him or her by:\n(c) the Commissioner; or\n(d) the AFP appointee under whose control, direction or\nsupervision he or she performs his or her duties.\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nAdministration and control etc.  Division 1\nSection 40A\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025",
      "skos:definition": "An AFP appointee must not:\n(a) disobey; or\n(b) fail to carry out;\na lawful direction, instruction or order, whether written or oral,\ngiven to him or her by:\n(c) the Commissioner; or\n(d) the AFP appointee under whose control, direction or\nsupervision he or she performs his or her duties.\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nAdministration and control etc.  Division 1\nSection 40A\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5ee25e3be8eafceaabb2f6f89be6e0e76fe971678a79d5e267db0a676f70e4e0",
      "skos:note": "Disobeying or failing to carry out lawful directions is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40 Compliance with specific directions, instructions or orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "An AFP appointee must not:\n(a) disobey; or\n(b) fail to carry out;\na lawful direction, instruction or order, whether written or oral,\ngiven to him or her by:\n(c) the Commissioner; or\n(d) the AFP appointee under whose control, direction or\nsupervision he or she performs his or her duties.\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nAdministration and control etc.  Division 1\nSection 40A\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of disobedience",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Lawful direction given by the Commissioner or AFP appointee",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Disobeying is prohibited"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40A Self-incrimination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an AFP appointee is required under section 39 or 40 to give\ninformation, answer a question or produce a document, he or she is\nnot excused from giving the information, answering the question or\nproducing the document on the ground that the information, the\nanswer to the question or the production of the document might\ntend to incriminate him or her or make him or her liable to a\npenalty.\n(2) However, any information or answer so given or any document so\nproduced is not admissible in evidence against the AFP appointee\nin any proceedings.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any information or answer so\ngiven, or any document so produced, that is relevant to conducting\na test under section 40M or 40N (about testing for alcohol or\nprohibited drugs)\nNote:\nSection 40Q deals with the admissibility of such information etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an AFP appointee is required under section 39 or 40 to give\ninformation, answer a question or produce a document, he or she is\nnot excused from giving the information, answering the question or\nproducing the document on the ground that the information, the\nanswer to the question or the production of the document might\ntend to incriminate him or her or make him or her liable to a\npenalty.\n(2) However, any information or answer so given or any document so\nproduced is not admissible in evidence against the AFP appointee\nin any proceedings.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any information or answer so\ngiven, or any document so produced, that is relevant to conducting\na test under section 40M or 40N (about testing for alcohol or\nprohibited drugs)\nNote:\nSection 40Q deals with the admissibility of such information etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "14eb48d5c86aea4919a06a4f9c3eacc9c80f1552a112268dccb212959bba1167"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40A Self-incrimination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an AFP appointee is required under section 39 or 40 to give\ninformation, answer a question or produce a document, he or she is\nnot excused from giving the information, answering the question or\nproducing the document on the ground that the information, the\nanswer to the question or the production of the document might\ntend to incriminate him or her or make him or her liable to a\npenalty.\n(2) However, any information or answer so given or any document so\nproduced is not admissible in evidence against the AFP appointee\nin any proceedings.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any information or answer so\ngiven, or any document so produced, that is relevant to conducting\na test under section 40M or 40N (about testing for alcohol or\nprohibited drugs)\nNote:\nSection 40Q deals with the admissibility of such information etc."
    },
