      "values:originalText": "(1) If an AFP appointee is required under section 39 or 40 to give\ninformation, answer a question or produce a document, he or she is\nnot excused from giving the information, answering the question or\nproducing the document on the ground that the information, the\nanswer to the question or the production of the document might\ntend to incriminate him or her or make him or her liable to a\npenalty.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an AFP appointee is required under section 39 or 40 to give\ninformation, answer a question or produce a document, he or she is\nnot excused from giving the information, answering the question or\nproducing the document on the ground that the information, the\nanswer to the question or the production of the document might\ntend to incriminate him or her or make him or her liable to a\npenalty.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40a"
