        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40D Commissioned police officers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "Commission by Governor-General\n(1) The Governor-General may, by commission, declare a member to\nbe a commissioned police officer.\n(2) Before the Governor-General makes a declaration under\nsubsection (1), the Minister must have received a recommendation\nfrom the Commissioner that the member be declared to be a\ncommissioned police officer.\n(3) The Commissioner may make such a recommendation only if he or\nshe is satisfied that the member is, in accordance with the\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nConferral of status of member and conferral of commissions  Division 2\nSection 40D\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nregulations, competent and qualified to be a commissioned police\nofficer.\nCommission by Commissioner or Deputy Commissioner\n(4) If the Governor-General, in writing, authorises the Commissioner\nor a Deputy Commissioner to make declarations of the kind\nmentioned in subsection (1), the Commissioner or Deputy\nCommissioner may, by commission, declare a member to be a\ncommissioned police officer.\n(5) The Commissioner or Deputy Commissioner may make a\ndeclaration under subsection (4) only if he or she is satisfied that\nthe member is, in accordance with the regulations, competent and\nqualified to be a commissioned police officer.\n(6) The giving of an authorisation under subsection (4) does not limit\nthe Governor-General’s power under subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "Commission by Governor-General\n(1) The Governor-General may, by commission, declare a member to\nbe a commissioned police officer.\n(2) Before the Governor-General makes a declaration under\nsubsection (1), the Minister must have received a recommendation\nfrom the Commissioner that the member be declared to be a\ncommissioned police officer.\n(3) The Commissioner may make such a recommendation only if he or\nshe is satisfied that the member is, in accordance with the\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nConferral of status of member and conferral of commissions  Division 2\nSection 40D\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nregulations, competent and qualified to be a commissioned police\nofficer.\nCommission by Commissioner or Deputy Commissioner\n(4) If the Governor-General, in writing, authorises the Commissioner\nor a Deputy Commissioner to make declarations of the kind\nmentioned in subsection (1), the Commissioner or Deputy\nCommissioner may, by commission, declare a member to be a\ncommissioned police officer.\n(5) The Commissioner or Deputy Commissioner may make a\ndeclaration under subsection (4) only if he or she is satisfied that\nthe member is, in accordance with the regulations, competent and\nqualified to be a commissioned police officer.\n(6) The giving of an authorisation under subsection (4) does not limit\nthe Governor-General’s power under subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40d-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40d-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40d-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dadfaba964dd0f38fb0585967ecf8836d954512cf427fa542dfea667abae2f14"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40D Commissioned police officers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "Commission by Governor-General\n(1) The Governor-General may, by commission, declare a member to\nbe a commissioned police officer.\n(2) Before the Governor-General makes a declaration under\nsubsection (1), the Minister must have received a recommendation\nfrom the Commissioner that the member be declared to be a\ncommissioned police officer.\n(3) The Commissioner may make such a recommendation only if he or\nshe is satisfied that the member is, in accordance with the\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nConferral of status of member and conferral of commissions  Division 2\nSection 40D\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nregulations, competent and qualified to be a commissioned police\nofficer.\nCommission by Commissioner or Deputy Commissioner\n(4) If the Governor-General, in writing, authorises the Commissioner\nor a Deputy Commissioner to make declarations of the kind\nmentioned in subsection (1), the Commissioner or Deputy\nCommissioner may, by commission, declare a member to be a\ncommissioned police officer.\n(5) The Commissioner or Deputy Commissioner may make a\ndeclaration under subsection (4) only if he or she is satisfied that\nthe member is, in accordance with the regulations, competent and\nqualified to be a commissioned police officer.\n(6) The giving of an authorisation under subsection (4) does not limit\nthe Governor-General’s power under subsection (1)."
    },
