    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40E Special members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may, on such terms and conditions as he or she\ndetermines in writing, appoint a person as a special member of the\nAustralian Federal Police to assist in the performance of its\nfunctions.\nNote:\nThe Commissioner may, under section 35A, authorise special\npayments to special members.\n(2) A person appointed under subsection (1) has, during the\ncontinuance of his or her appointment:\n(a) any powers and duties that are expressly conferred or\nimposed on special members under a provision of this Act or\nof any other Act; and\n(b) such of the powers and duties conferred or imposed on\nmembers as are specified in his or her instrument of\nappointment.\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nConferral of status of protective service officer  Division 3A\nSection 40EA\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may, on such terms and conditions as he or she\ndetermines in writing, appoint a person as a special member of the\nAustralian Federal Police to assist in the performance of its\nfunctions.\nNote:\nThe Commissioner may, under section 35A, authorise special\npayments to special members.\n(2) A person appointed under subsection (1) has, during the\ncontinuance of his or her appointment:\n(a) any powers and duties that are expressly conferred or\nimposed on special members under a provision of this Act or\nof any other Act; and\n(b) such of the powers and duties conferred or imposed on\nmembers as are specified in his or her instrument of\nappointment.\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nConferral of status of protective service officer  Division 3A\nSection 40EA\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40e-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "892884cf56d33c8ea241737857c0873798559ddc69d3b4f2f499c8e6f35c704b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40E Special members",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may, on such terms and conditions as he or she\ndetermines in writing, appoint a person as a special member of the\nAustralian Federal Police to assist in the performance of its\nfunctions.\nNote:\nThe Commissioner may, under section 35A, authorise special\npayments to special members.\n(2) A person appointed under subsection (1) has, during the\ncontinuance of his or her appointment:\n(a) any powers and duties that are expressly conferred or\nimposed on special members under a provision of this Act or\nof any other Act; and\n(b) such of the powers and duties conferred or imposed on\nmembers as are specified in his or her instrument of\nappointment.\n\n\nCommissioner’s command powers etc.  Part IV\nConferral of status of protective service officer  Division 3A\nSection 40EA\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025"
    },
