      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the\nduties of an AFP employee, and the place or places at which the\nduties are to be performed.\nDetermination of terms and conditions while AFP employee\noutside Australia\n(2) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the\nterms and conditions applying to an AFP employee while the\nemployee is performing duties outside Australia.\nDuties to meet special operational needs\n(3) If:\n(a) the Commissioner makes a determination under\nsubsection (1); and\n(b) the Commissioner specifies in the determination that the\nduties concerned are to meet the special operational needs of\nthe Australian Federal Police;\nthe Commissioner may determine in writing the accommodation\narrangements that are to apply to the employee, or any allowances\nthe employee is to be paid, while the employee is performing those\nduties.\n(4) Without limiting subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901, the Commissioner may at any time revoke in writing a\ndetermination made under subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the\nduties of an AFP employee, and the place or places at which the\nduties are to be performed.\nDetermination of terms and conditions while AFP employee\noutside Australia\n(2) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the\nterms and conditions applying to an AFP employee while the\nemployee is performing duties outside Australia.\nDuties to meet special operational needs\n(3) If:\n(a) the Commissioner makes a determination under\nsubsection (1); and\n(b) the Commissioner specifies in the determination that the\nduties concerned are to meet the special operational needs of\nthe Australian Federal Police;\nthe Commissioner may determine in writing the accommodation\narrangements that are to apply to the employee, or any allowances\nthe employee is to be paid, while the employee is performing those\nduties.\n(4) Without limiting subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901, the Commissioner may at any time revoke in writing a\ndetermination made under subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40h-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40h-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fb60f1b69d5eeae3b548f10990e5348b5d9b6e1827997d82caa0a65147b4791c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40H Assignment of duties etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 83,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the\nduties of an AFP employee, and the place or places at which the\nduties are to be performed.\nDetermination of terms and conditions while AFP employee\noutside Australia\n(2) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the\nterms and conditions applying to an AFP employee while the\nemployee is performing duties outside Australia.\nDuties to meet special operational needs\n(3) If:\n(a) the Commissioner makes a determination under\nsubsection (1); and\n(b) the Commissioner specifies in the determination that the\nduties concerned are to meet the special operational needs of\nthe Australian Federal Police;\nthe Commissioner may determine in writing the accommodation\narrangements that are to apply to the employee, or any allowances\nthe employee is to be paid, while the employee is performing those\nduties.\n(4) Without limiting subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901, the Commissioner may at any time revoke in writing a\ndetermination made under subsection (1)."
    },
