    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40L Financial statements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.87",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may give a person who is an AFP employee or\na special member a written direction requiring the person to give\nthe Commissioner a statement in accordance with subsection (2).\nNature etc. of statement\n(2) The statement must:\n(a) be made in a form and manner required by the\nCommissioner; and\n(b) contain any information required by the Commissioner about\nthe financial affairs of the person during a period, or each\nperiod, specified by the Commissioner; and\n(c) be accompanied by any documents required by the\nCommissioner.\nTime limit for giving statement\n(3) The person must give the statement to the Commissioner within 2\nmonths after the end of the period to which the statement relates.\nExtension of time\n(4) The Commissioner may grant an extension of time for giving the\nstatement in special circumstances.\nSelf-incrimination\n(5) The person is not excused from giving the statement on the ground\nthat the statement might tend to incriminate him or her or make\nhim or her liable to a penalty.\n(6) However, any statement so given is not admissible in evidence\nagainst the person in any proceedings.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may give a person who is an AFP employee or\na special member a written direction requiring the person to give\nthe Commissioner a statement in accordance with subsection (2).\nNature etc. of statement\n(2) The statement must:\n(a) be made in a form and manner required by the\nCommissioner; and\n(b) contain any information required by the Commissioner about\nthe financial affairs of the person during a period, or each\nperiod, specified by the Commissioner; and\n(c) be accompanied by any documents required by the\nCommissioner.\nTime limit for giving statement\n(3) The person must give the statement to the Commissioner within 2\nmonths after the end of the period to which the statement relates.\nExtension of time\n(4) The Commissioner may grant an extension of time for giving the\nstatement in special circumstances.\nSelf-incrimination\n(5) The person is not excused from giving the statement on the ground\nthat the statement might tend to incriminate him or her or make\nhim or her liable to a penalty.\n(6) However, any statement so given is not admissible in evidence\nagainst the person in any proceedings.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40l-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40l-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40l-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40l-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40l-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d7db2f7bb421082079f6d1a6b08e014d7cc22eb5b144048d6954fbe5079b1c12"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40L Financial statements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may give a person who is an AFP employee or\na special member a written direction requiring the person to give\nthe Commissioner a statement in accordance with subsection (2).\nNature etc. of statement\n(2) The statement must:\n(a) be made in a form and manner required by the\nCommissioner; and\n(b) contain any information required by the Commissioner about\nthe financial affairs of the person during a period, or each\nperiod, specified by the Commissioner; and\n(c) be accompanied by any documents required by the\nCommissioner.\nTime limit for giving statement\n(3) The person must give the statement to the Commissioner within 2\nmonths after the end of the period to which the statement relates.\nExtension of time\n(4) The Commissioner may grant an extension of time for giving the\nstatement in special circumstances.\nSelf-incrimination\n(5) The person is not excused from giving the statement on the ground\nthat the statement might tend to incriminate him or her or make\nhim or her liable to a penalty.\n(6) However, any statement so given is not admissible in evidence\nagainst the person in any proceedings."
    },
