    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40RC Commissioner may determine professional standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40rc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.97",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may issue Commissioner’s orders under\nsection 38 determining the professional standards to be complied\nwith by AFP appointees.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner may determine\na professional standard by reference to the requirements specified\nin:\n(a) another Commissioner’s order; or\n(b) another document issued or made by the Commissioner in\nthe exercise of the Commissioner’s powers under section 37.\n(3) Despite section 46AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, a\ndocument referred to in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) may be a document:\n(a) as in force at a particular time; or\n(b) as in force from time to time.\nSubdivision C—Unit within Australian Federal Police to\nundertake professional standards functions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may issue Commissioner’s orders under\nsection 38 determining the professional standards to be complied\nwith by AFP appointees.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner may determine\na professional standard by reference to the requirements specified\nin:\n(a) another Commissioner’s order; or\n(b) another document issued or made by the Commissioner in\nthe exercise of the Commissioner’s powers under section 37.\n(3) Despite section 46AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, a\ndocument referred to in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) may be a document:\n(a) as in force at a particular time; or\n(b) as in force from time to time.\nSubdivision C—Unit within Australian Federal Police to\nundertake professional standards functions",
