    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40RF Assignment of members, and special members, to unit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40rf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, assign a member, or special\nmember, of the Australian Federal Police to the unit constituted\nunder section 40RD.\n(2) The assignment must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) specify the period during which the member, or special\nmember, is to serve in the unit.\n(3) The period specified under paragraph (2)(b) must not exceed 2\nyears.\n(4) If the Commissioner is satisfied that there are special reasons for\ndoing so, the Commissioner may vary, or further vary, the\nassignment under subsection (1) by substituting for the period\nspecified in the assignment a shorter or longer period.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RG\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(5) The period substituted under subsection (4) may exceed 2 years.\n(6) As soon as practicable after the member, or special member, has\nserved in the unit for the period specified in the assignment, the\nCommissioner must arrange for the member, or special member, to\ncease serving in the unit.\n(7) If:\n(a) a member, or special member, of the Australian Federal\nPolice is assigned to the unit constituted under section 40RD;\nand\n(b) the member, or special member, ceases to serve in the unit;\nand\n(c) the period of 12 months from the time when the member, or\nspecial member, ceased to serve in the unit ends;\nthe member, or special member, may again be assigned to the unit.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, assign a member, or special\nmember, of the Australian Federal Police to the unit constituted\nunder section 40RD.\n(2) The assignment must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) specify the period during which the member, or special\nmember, is to serve in the unit.\n(3) The period specified under paragraph (2)(b) must not exceed 2\nyears.\n(4) If the Commissioner is satisfied that there are special reasons for\ndoing so, the Commissioner may vary, or further vary, the\nassignment under subsection (1) by substituting for the period\nspecified in the assignment a shorter or longer period.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RG\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(5) The period substituted under subsection (4) may exceed 2 years.\n(6) As soon as practicable after the member, or special member, has\nserved in the unit for the period specified in the assignment, the\nCommissioner must arrange for the member, or special member, to\ncease serving in the unit.\n(7) If:\n(a) a member, or special member, of the Australian Federal\nPolice is assigned to the unit constituted under section 40RD;\nand\n(b) the member, or special member, ceases to serve in the unit;\nand\n(c) the period of 12 months from the time when the member, or\nspecial member, ceased to serve in the unit ends;\nthe member, or special member, may again be assigned to the unit.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rf-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rf-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rf-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rf-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rf-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rf-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ffd617f468b5c1369ec7606d36a8a28904f4a36dab071aca195c0e48b87b6c3d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40rf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40RF Assignment of members, and special members, to unit",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, assign a member, or special\nmember, of the Australian Federal Police to the unit constituted\nunder section 40RD.\n(2) The assignment must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) specify the period during which the member, or special\nmember, is to serve in the unit.\n(3) The period specified under paragraph (2)(b) must not exceed 2\nyears.\n(4) If the Commissioner is satisfied that there are special reasons for\ndoing so, the Commissioner may vary, or further vary, the\nassignment under subsection (1) by substituting for the period\nspecified in the assignment a shorter or longer period.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RG\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(5) The period substituted under subsection (4) may exceed 2 years.\n(6) As soon as practicable after the member, or special member, has\nserved in the unit for the period specified in the assignment, the\nCommissioner must arrange for the member, or special member, to\ncease serving in the unit.\n(7) If:\n(a) a member, or special member, of the Australian Federal\nPolice is assigned to the unit constituted under section 40RD;\nand\n(b) the member, or special member, ceases to serve in the unit;\nand\n(c) the period of 12 months from the time when the member, or\nspecial member, ceased to serve in the unit ends;\nthe member, or special member, may again be assigned to the unit."
    },
