    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ri",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40RI AFP practices issues",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40ri"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, an AFP practices issue is an issue\nabout the practices or procedures of the Australian Federal Police\n(whether those practices or procedures are carried out within, or\noutside, Australia).\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an AFP practices issue includes\nan issue of whether a practice or procedure of the Australian\nFederal Police is or has been:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RJ\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) contrary to law; or\n(b) unreasonable, unjust, oppressive or improperly\ndiscriminatory; or\n(c) inadequate; or\n(d) otherwise wrong or inappropriate.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act, the practices or procedures of the\nAustralian Federal Police include:\n(a) the rules, orders and instructions (including the\nCommissioner’s Orders) in accordance with which AFP\nappointees are required to perform their duties; and\n(b) the policies adopted or followed by the Australian Federal\nPolice; and\n(c) the practices and procedures ordinarily followed by AFP\nappointees in the performance of their duties.\n(4) This section has effect subject to section 40RJ.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, an AFP practices issue is an issue\nabout the practices or procedures of the Australian Federal Police\n(whether those practices or procedures are carried out within, or\noutside, Australia).\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an AFP practices issue includes\nan issue of whether a practice or procedure of the Australian\nFederal Police is or has been:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RJ\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) contrary to law; or\n(b) unreasonable, unjust, oppressive or improperly\ndiscriminatory; or\n(c) inadequate; or\n(d) otherwise wrong or inappropriate.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act, the practices or procedures of the\nAustralian Federal Police include:\n(a) the rules, orders and instructions (including the\nCommissioner’s Orders) in accordance with which AFP\nappointees are required to perform their duties; and\n(b) the policies adopted or followed by the Australian Federal\nPolice; and\n(c) the practices and procedures ordinarily followed by AFP\nappointees in the performance of their duties.\n(4) This section has effect subject to section 40RJ.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ri-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ri-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ri-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ri-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "13589864ebf70cf935679d1fed5ea832f5aae569bd86bda3ebeb786a5f2c172b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40ri",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40RI AFP practices issues",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, an AFP practices issue is an issue\nabout the practices or procedures of the Australian Federal Police\n(whether those practices or procedures are carried out within, or\noutside, Australia).\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an AFP practices issue includes\nan issue of whether a practice or procedure of the Australian\nFederal Police is or has been:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RJ\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) contrary to law; or\n(b) unreasonable, unjust, oppressive or improperly\ndiscriminatory; or\n(c) inadequate; or\n(d) otherwise wrong or inappropriate.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act, the practices or procedures of the\nAustralian Federal Police include:\n(a) the rules, orders and instructions (including the\nCommissioner’s Orders) in accordance with which AFP\nappointees are required to perform their duties; and\n(b) the policies adopted or followed by the Australian Federal\nPolice; and\n(c) the practices and procedures ordinarily followed by AFP\nappointees in the performance of their duties.\n(4) This section has effect subject to section 40RJ."
    },
