    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40RM AFP Commissioner and Ombudsman to determine the kinds",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40rm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.103",
      "values:originalText": "of conduct that are to be category 1, category 2 or\ncategory 3 conduct\n(1) Subject to sections 40RN, 40RO and 40RP, the Commissioner and\nthe Ombudsman may jointly determine, by legislative instrument:\n(a) the kind of conduct that is to be category 1 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act; and\n(b) the kind of conduct that is to be category 2 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act; and\n(c) the kind of conduct that is to be category 3 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act.\n(2) If there is no determination under subsection (1) that applies to\nparticular conduct, the conduct is to be taken to be category 3\nconduct for the purposes of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "of conduct that are to be category 1, category 2 or\ncategory 3 conduct\n(1) Subject to sections 40RN, 40RO and 40RP, the Commissioner and\nthe Ombudsman may jointly determine, by legislative instrument:\n(a) the kind of conduct that is to be category 1 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act; and\n(b) the kind of conduct that is to be category 2 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act; and\n(c) the kind of conduct that is to be category 3 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act.\n(2) If there is no determination under subsection (1) that applies to\nparticular conduct, the conduct is to be taken to be category 3\nconduct for the purposes of this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rm-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rm-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "90fa95c6cbf859afbacaf94791a0285493d6ca4abf993dc392d5993d4a1459ff"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40rm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40RM AFP Commissioner and Ombudsman to determine the kinds",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 103,
      "values:originalText": "of conduct that are to be category 1, category 2 or\ncategory 3 conduct\n(1) Subject to sections 40RN, 40RO and 40RP, the Commissioner and\nthe Ombudsman may jointly determine, by legislative instrument:\n(a) the kind of conduct that is to be category 1 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act; and\n(b) the kind of conduct that is to be category 2 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act; and\n(c) the kind of conduct that is to be category 3 conduct for the\npurposes of this Act.\n(2) If there is no determination under subsection (1) that applies to\nparticular conduct, the conduct is to be taken to be category 3\nconduct for the purposes of this Act."
    },
