    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rp",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40RP Category 3 conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40rp"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman may determine under\nsubsection 40RM(1) that conduct of a particular kind is to be\ncategory 3 conduct for the purposes of this Act only if they are\nsatisfied that:\n(a) conduct of that kind:\n(i) is serious misconduct by an AFP appointee; or\n(ii) raises the question whether termination action should be\ntaken in relation to an AFP appointee; or\n(iii) involves a breach of the criminal law, or serious neglect\nof duty, by an AFP appointee; and\n(b) conduct of that kind does not raise a corruption issue.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RQ\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(2) Subparagraphs (1)(a)(ii) and (iii) do not limit\nsubparagraph (1)(a)(i).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman may determine under\nsubsection 40RM(1) that conduct of a particular kind is to be\ncategory 3 conduct for the purposes of this Act only if they are\nsatisfied that:\n(a) conduct of that kind:\n(i) is serious misconduct by an AFP appointee; or\n(ii) raises the question whether termination action should be\ntaken in relation to an AFP appointee; or\n(iii) involves a breach of the criminal law, or serious neglect\nof duty, by an AFP appointee; and\n(b) conduct of that kind does not raise a corruption issue.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RQ\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(2) Subparagraphs (1)(a)(ii) and (iii) do not limit\nsubparagraph (1)(a)(i).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rp-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rp-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e061f72e8cbc61b9ca645d9ca5965eaa94a006e24c679aa2a8b5e4805c6d9813"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40rp",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40RP Category 3 conduct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 104,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman may determine under\nsubsection 40RM(1) that conduct of a particular kind is to be\ncategory 3 conduct for the purposes of this Act only if they are\nsatisfied that:\n(a) conduct of that kind:\n(i) is serious misconduct by an AFP appointee; or\n(ii) raises the question whether termination action should be\ntaken in relation to an AFP appointee; or\n(iii) involves a breach of the criminal law, or serious neglect\nof duty, by an AFP appointee; and\n(b) conduct of that kind does not raise a corruption issue.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nPreliminary  Division 1\nSection 40RQ\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(2) Subparagraphs (1)(a)(ii) and (iii) do not limit\nsubparagraph (1)(a)(i)."
    },
