    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40sc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40SC Recording and dealing with information given under",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40sc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.109",
      "values:originalText": "section 40SA\n(1) If a person gives information to another person (the recipient)\nunder section 40SA, the recipient must:\n(a) record the details of the information; and\n(b) deal with the information in accordance with the\nCommissioner’s orders issued for the purposes of\nsubsection 40TA(1).\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the issue to which the information relates is:\n(i) a category 1 conduct issue; or\n(ii) an AFP practices issue; and\n(b) the recipient is satisfied that the issue:\n(i) arises as a result of a misunderstanding of the facts, the\nlaw or the practices or procedures of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n(ii) is otherwise appropriate for informal resolution; and\n(c) the recipient is satisfied that:\n(i) giving an explanation to the person giving the\ninformation; or\n(ii) taking other action;\nis likely to resolve the issue; and\n(d) the recipient is satisfied that the recipient is able to give the\nperson giving the information that explanation, or arrange for\nthat action to be taken, within a reasonable period.\n(3) If the issue is not resolved within a reasonable period, the recipient\nmust:\n(a) record the details of the information; and",
      "skos:definition": "section 40SA\n(1) If a person gives information to another person (the recipient)\nunder section 40SA, the recipient must:\n(a) record the details of the information; and\n(b) deal with the information in accordance with the\nCommissioner’s orders issued for the purposes of\nsubsection 40TA(1).\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the issue to which the information relates is:\n(i) a category 1 conduct issue; or\n(ii) an AFP practices issue; and\n(b) the recipient is satisfied that the issue:\n(i) arises as a result of a misunderstanding of the facts, the\nlaw or the practices or procedures of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n(ii) is otherwise appropriate for informal resolution; and\n(c) the recipient is satisfied that:\n(i) giving an explanation to the person giving the\ninformation; or\n(ii) taking other action;\nis likely to resolve the issue; and\n(d) the recipient is satisfied that the recipient is able to give the\nperson giving the information that explanation, or arrange for\nthat action to be taken, within a reasonable period.\n(3) If the issue is not resolved within a reasonable period, the recipient\nmust:\n(a) record the details of the information; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40sc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40sc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40sc-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5f19401477e06ae517a71473e587d99b1f36253331d2b774200935c8bddee31"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40sc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40SC Recording and dealing with information given under",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 109,
      "values:originalText": "section 40SA\n(1) If a person gives information to another person (the recipient)\nunder section 40SA, the recipient must:\n(a) record the details of the information; and\n(b) deal with the information in accordance with the\nCommissioner’s orders issued for the purposes of\nsubsection 40TA(1).\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the issue to which the information relates is:\n(i) a category 1 conduct issue; or\n(ii) an AFP practices issue; and\n(b) the recipient is satisfied that the issue:\n(i) arises as a result of a misunderstanding of the facts, the\nlaw or the practices or procedures of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n(ii) is otherwise appropriate for informal resolution; and\n(c) the recipient is satisfied that:\n(i) giving an explanation to the person giving the\ninformation; or\n(ii) taking other action;\nis likely to resolve the issue; and\n(d) the recipient is satisfied that the recipient is able to give the\nperson giving the information that explanation, or arrange for\nthat action to be taken, within a reasonable period.\n(3) If the issue is not resolved within a reasonable period, the recipient\nmust:\n(a) record the details of the information; and"
    },
    {
