    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40td",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40TD Remedial action",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40td"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, remedial action in relation to an AFP\nappointee is action taken to remedy unsatisfactory performance by\nthe AFP appointee.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), remedial action in relation to the\nAFP appointee may include one or more of the following:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TE\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) action taken to improve the AFP appointee’s behaviour;\n(b) structured changes to the AFP appointee’s employment;\n(c) the recording of adverse findings against the AFP appointee\n(whether for a particular period or permanently).\n(3) Without limiting paragraph (2)(a), remedial action in relation to\nthe AFP appointee may take one or more of the following forms:\n(a) counselling the AFP appointee or arranging for the AFP\nappointee to be counselled;\n(b) reprimanding the AFP appointee;\n(c) giving the AFP appointee a formal warning;\n(d) requiring the AFP appointee to adopt particular improvement\nstrategies.\n(4) Without limiting paragraph (2)(b), remedial action in relation to\nthe AFP appointee may take one or more of the following forms:\n(a) changing the AFP appointee’s shifts or arranging for or\nrecommending such a change;\n(b) restricting the AFP appointee’s duties or arranging for or\nrecommending such a restriction;\n(c) reassigning the AFP appointee to other duties or arranging\nfor or recommending such a reassignment;\n(d) transferring the AFP appointee to another part of the\nAustralian Federal Police or arranging for or recommending\nsuch a transfer.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, remedial action in relation to an AFP\nappointee is action taken to remedy unsatisfactory performance by\nthe AFP appointee.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), remedial action in relation to the\nAFP appointee may include one or more of the following:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TE\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) action taken to improve the AFP appointee’s behaviour;\n(b) structured changes to the AFP appointee’s employment;\n(c) the recording of adverse findings against the AFP appointee\n(whether for a particular period or permanently).\n(3) Without limiting paragraph (2)(a), remedial action in relation to\nthe AFP appointee may take one or more of the following forms:\n(a) counselling the AFP appointee or arranging for the AFP\nappointee to be counselled;\n(b) reprimanding the AFP appointee;\n(c) giving the AFP appointee a formal warning;\n(d) requiring the AFP appointee to adopt particular improvement\nstrategies.\n(4) Without limiting paragraph (2)(b), remedial action in relation to\nthe AFP appointee may take one or more of the following forms:\n(a) changing the AFP appointee’s shifts or arranging for or\nrecommending such a change;\n(b) restricting the AFP appointee’s duties or arranging for or\nrecommending such a restriction;\n(c) reassigning the AFP appointee to other duties or arranging\nfor or recommending such a reassignment;\n(d) transferring the AFP appointee to another part of the\nAustralian Federal Police or arranging for or recommending\nsuch a transfer.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40td-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40td-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40td-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40td-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "360854e1c51fa4a73a3c13a182deef0c79bfc052bd1f5609294140fe2aac8fb0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40td",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40TD Remedial action",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, remedial action in relation to an AFP\nappointee is action taken to remedy unsatisfactory performance by\nthe AFP appointee.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), remedial action in relation to the\nAFP appointee may include one or more of the following:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TE\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) action taken to improve the AFP appointee’s behaviour;\n(b) structured changes to the AFP appointee’s employment;\n(c) the recording of adverse findings against the AFP appointee\n(whether for a particular period or permanently).\n(3) Without limiting paragraph (2)(a), remedial action in relation to\nthe AFP appointee may take one or more of the following forms:\n(a) counselling the AFP appointee or arranging for the AFP\nappointee to be counselled;\n(b) reprimanding the AFP appointee;\n(c) giving the AFP appointee a formal warning;\n(d) requiring the AFP appointee to adopt particular improvement\nstrategies.\n(4) Without limiting paragraph (2)(b), remedial action in relation to\nthe AFP appointee may take one or more of the following forms:\n(a) changing the AFP appointee’s shifts or arranging for or\nrecommending such a change;\n(b) restricting the AFP appointee’s duties or arranging for or\nrecommending such a restriction;\n(c) reassigning the AFP appointee to other duties or arranging\nfor or recommending such a reassignment;\n(d) transferring the AFP appointee to another part of the\nAustralian Federal Police or arranging for or recommending\nsuch a transfer."
    },
