    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40TF Discretion to take no further action in relation to AFP conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40tf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.115",
      "values:originalText": "or practices issue\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) a person gives information under section 40SA that raises:\n(i) an AFP conduct issue in relation to conduct engaged in\nby an AFP appointee; or\n(ii) an AFP practices issue in relation to a practice or\nprocedure of the AFP; or\n(b) the Commissioner decides under section 40SD that an AFP\nconduct issue in relation to an AFP appointee is to be dealt\nwith under this Part.\n(2) The Commissioner may determine that no further action is to be\ntaken under this Part in relation to the issue if the Commissioner is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the person became aware of the conduct, or the practice or\nprocedure, more than 12 months before the person gave the\ninformation under section 40SA; or\n(b) appropriate action has already been taken:\n(i) against the AFP appointee in relation to the conduct; or\n(ii) in relation to the practice or procedure; or",
      "skos:definition": "or practices issue\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) a person gives information under section 40SA that raises:\n(i) an AFP conduct issue in relation to conduct engaged in\nby an AFP appointee; or\n(ii) an AFP practices issue in relation to a practice or\nprocedure of the AFP; or\n(b) the Commissioner decides under section 40SD that an AFP\nconduct issue in relation to an AFP appointee is to be dealt\nwith under this Part.\n(2) The Commissioner may determine that no further action is to be\ntaken under this Part in relation to the issue if the Commissioner is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the person became aware of the conduct, or the practice or\nprocedure, more than 12 months before the person gave the\ninformation under section 40SA; or\n(b) appropriate action has already been taken:\n(i) against the AFP appointee in relation to the conduct; or\n(ii) in relation to the practice or procedure; or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tf-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b14473a63b9a0f0430b241b99c6718cd8470193056f0a97bf19865c5c376237b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40tf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40TF Discretion to take no further action in relation to AFP conduct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "or practices issue\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) a person gives information under section 40SA that raises:\n(i) an AFP conduct issue in relation to conduct engaged in\nby an AFP appointee; or\n(ii) an AFP practices issue in relation to a practice or\nprocedure of the AFP; or\n(b) the Commissioner decides under section 40SD that an AFP\nconduct issue in relation to an AFP appointee is to be dealt\nwith under this Part.\n(2) The Commissioner may determine that no further action is to be\ntaken under this Part in relation to the issue if the Commissioner is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the person became aware of the conduct, or the practice or\nprocedure, more than 12 months before the person gave the\ninformation under section 40SA; or\n(b) appropriate action has already been taken:\n(i) against the AFP appointee in relation to the conduct; or\n(ii) in relation to the practice or procedure; or"
    },
