      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Commissioner may determine no further action is to be taken if appropriate action has already been taken.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) appropriate action has already been taken:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tf-ss-2-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Commissioner may determine no further action is to be taken if the person gave information under section 40SA more than 12 months after becoming aware of the conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the person became aware of the conduct, or the practice or procedure, more than 12 months before the person gave the information under section 40SA;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40th",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40TH How issue is dealt with",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40th"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.117",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In dealing with the AFP conduct issue, the manager must:\n(a) ensure that:\n(i) the AFP appointee; and\n(ii) the complainant (if any);\nhave an adequate opportunity to be heard in relation to the\nissue; and\n(b) ensure that the AFP appointee is involved, as far as\npracticable, in the resolution of the issue; and\n(c) determine what action (if any) is to be taken under\nsection 40TI or 40TJ in relation to the issue; and\n(d) consider whether the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue.\nNote:\nParagraph (d)—see also section 40TK.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In dealing with the AFP conduct issue, the manager must:\n(a) ensure that:\n(i) the AFP appointee; and\n(ii) the complainant (if any);\nhave an adequate opportunity to be heard in relation to the\nissue; and\n(b) ensure that the AFP appointee is involved, as far as\npracticable, in the resolution of the issue; and\n(c) determine what action (if any) is to be taken under\nsection 40TI or 40TJ in relation to the issue; and\n(d) consider whether the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue.\nNote:\nParagraph (d)—see also section 40TK.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40th-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40th-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40th-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40th-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6e74e4942f7ee147b1cfad559b7aa20dec520db64eaf1e530583471b8d608336",
      "skos:note": "Ensure adequate opportunity for AFP appointee and complainant to be heard in relation to the issue."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40th",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40TH How issue is dealt with",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 117,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In dealing with the AFP conduct issue, the manager must:\n(a) ensure that:\n(i) the AFP appointee; and\n(ii) the complainant (if any);\nhave an adequate opportunity to be heard in relation to the\nissue; and\n(b) ensure that the AFP appointee is involved, as far as\npracticable, in the resolution of the issue; and\n(c) determine what action (if any) is to be taken under\nsection 40TI or 40TJ in relation to the issue; and\n(d) consider whether the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue.\nNote:\nParagraph (d)—see also section 40TK."
    },
