      "cml:premiseText": "(1) In dealing with the AFP conduct issue, the manager must:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ti",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40TI Action that may be taken in relation to category 1 conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40ti"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "If the manager is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 1 conduct, the manager may\ntake training and development action in relation to the AFP\nappointee.\nNote:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC.",
      "skos:definition": "If the manager is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 1 conduct, the manager may\ntake training and development action in relation to the AFP\nappointee.\nNote:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ti-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ti-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6d3cd180c907ee7998772ec9fe662b4d862d556f29b0088bccad2b5c3a1f6cd4",
      "skos:note": "Manager must take training and development action if satisfied category 1 conduct has occurred."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40ti",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40TI Action that may be taken in relation to category 1 conduct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "If the manager is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 1 conduct, the manager may\ntake training and development action in relation to the AFP\nappointee.\nNote:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ti-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ti"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ti-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Manager must take action",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40TJ Action that may be taken in relation to category 2 conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40tj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "If the manager is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 2 conduct, the manager may do\neither or both of the following:\n(a) take remedial action in relation to the AFP appointee;\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TK\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(b) take training and development action in relation to the AFP\nappointee.\nNote 1:\nFor remedial action, see section 40TD.\nNote 2:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC.",
      "skos:definition": "If the manager is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 2 conduct, the manager may do\neither or both of the following:\n(a) take remedial action in relation to the AFP appointee;\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TK\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(b) take training and development action in relation to the AFP\nappointee.\nNote 1:\nFor remedial action, see section 40TD.\nNote 2:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tj-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tj-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "34c08ea9f3ebf3f3c571c3f39dd25b659ebb4d88f4c901cc52f5923a1b91d1e7",
      "skos:note": "Action that may be taken in relation to category 2 conduct"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40tj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40TJ Action that may be taken in relation to category 2 conduct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "If the manager is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 2 conduct, the manager may do\neither or both of the following:\n(a) take remedial action in relation to the AFP appointee;\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TK\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(b) take training and development action in relation to the AFP\nappointee.\nNote 1:\nFor remedial action, see section 40TD.\nNote 2:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tj-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
