    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40to-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40TO(6) Commissioner must allocate issue to someone outside unit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40to-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.121",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n(a) the issue is a category 3 conduct issue; and\n(b) the Commissioner allocates the issue under subsection (2) to\nsomeone other than the Ombudsman;\nthe Commissioner must consult with the Ombudsman about the\nchoice of the person to whom the issue is to be allocated.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If:\n(a) the issue is a category 3 conduct issue; and\n(b) the Commissioner allocates the issue under subsection (2) to\nsomeone other than the Ombudsman;\nthe Commissioner must consult with the Ombudsman about the\nchoice of the person to whom the issue is to be allocated.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40to"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40to-ss-6-norm"
        },
