      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.122",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the issue is allocated to a person under\nsection 40TN or 40TO.\n(2) In investigating the issue, the investigator must:\n(a) ensure that:\n(i) the AFP appointee; and\n(ii) the complainant (if any);\nhave, subject to the requirements of the investigation, an\nadequate opportunity to be heard in relation to the issue; and\n(b) consider whether the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the issue is allocated to a person under\nsection 40TN or 40TO.\n(2) In investigating the issue, the investigator must:\n(a) ensure that:\n(i) the AFP appointee; and\n(ii) the complainant (if any);\nhave, subject to the requirements of the investigation, an\nadequate opportunity to be heard in relation to the issue; and\n(b) consider whether the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue.",
