    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40tq-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40TQ(2) How category 3 conduct issue or corruption issue is dealt with",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 122,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In investigating the issue, the investigator must:\n(a) ensure that:\n(i) the AFP appointee; and\n(ii) the complainant (if any);\nhave, subject to the requirements of the investigation, an\nadequate opportunity to be heard in relation to the issue; and\n(b) consider whether the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tq-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
