      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.122",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the investigator is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 3 conduct or corrupt conduct,\nthe investigator may recommend that any one or more of the\nfollowing be taken in relation to the AFP appointee:\n(a) termination action;\n(b) remedial action;\n(c) training and development action;\n(d) any other action that the Commissioner can take in relation to\nthe AFP appointee.\nNote 1:\nFor termination action, see section 40TE.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TS\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nNote 2:\nFor remedial action, see section 40TD.\nNote 3:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC.\nNote 4:\nIf evidence emerges, at any stage of the investigation, that the AFP\nappointee may have committed an offence, the investigator could also\narrange for the AFP appointee to be charged with the offence. This\nmight be done even before the investigation of the issue is completed.\nThe AFP appointee might be charged with the offence even if the\ninvestigator does not recommend that termination, remedial or\ntraining and development action to be taken in relation to the AFP\nappointee.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the investigator is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 3 conduct or corrupt conduct,\nthe investigator may recommend that any one or more of the\nfollowing be taken in relation to the AFP appointee:\n(a) termination action;\n(b) remedial action;\n(c) training and development action;\n(d) any other action that the Commissioner can take in relation to\nthe AFP appointee.\nNote 1:\nFor termination action, see section 40TE.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TS\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nNote 2:\nFor remedial action, see section 40TD.\nNote 3:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC.\nNote 4:\nIf evidence emerges, at any stage of the investigation, that the AFP\nappointee may have committed an offence, the investigator could also\narrange for the AFP appointee to be charged with the offence. This\nmight be done even before the investigation of the issue is completed.\nThe AFP appointee might be charged with the offence even if the\ninvestigator does not recommend that termination, remedial or\ntraining and development action to be taken in relation to the AFP\nappointee.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tr"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tr-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tr-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tr-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tr-ss-1-logic-linearlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tr-ss-1-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tr-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "024c7d9efa73e87c22ba0e319a91fda0034ee7eeebeb47b409350dbb762b7c62",
      "skos:note": "The investigator may recommend one or more actions to be taken in relation to the AFP appointee."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40tr-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40TR(1) Recommendations that may be made in relation to category 3",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 122,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the investigator is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the AFP\nappointee has engaged in category 3 conduct or corrupt conduct,\nthe investigator may recommend that any one or more of the\nfollowing be taken in relation to the AFP appointee:\n(a) termination action;\n(b) remedial action;\n(c) training and development action;\n(d) any other action that the Commissioner can take in relation to\nthe AFP appointee.\nNote 1:\nFor termination action, see section 40TE.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TS\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nNote 2:\nFor remedial action, see section 40TD.\nNote 3:\nFor training and development action, see section 40TC.\nNote 4:\nIf evidence emerges, at any stage of the investigation, that the AFP\nappointee may have committed an offence, the investigator could also\narrange for the AFP appointee to be charged with the offence. This\nmight be done even before the investigation of the issue is completed.\nThe AFP appointee might be charged with the offence even if the\ninvestigator does not recommend that termination, remedial or\ntraining and development action to be taken in relation to the AFP\nappointee."
    },
