    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tw",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40TW AFP practices issue identified in course of dealing with AFP",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40tw"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.124",
      "values:originalText": "conduct issue\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the investigator is satisfied that the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue; and\n(b) the investigator prepares a report under section 40TU in\nrelation to the investigation.\n(2) The investigator:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TX\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) must identify the AFP practices issue in the report; and\n(b) may include in the report such recommendations as the\ninvestigator considers appropriate to address the AFP\npractices issue.\nSubdivision E—Dealing with AFP practices issues",
      "skos:definition": "conduct issue\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the investigator is satisfied that the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue; and\n(b) the investigator prepares a report under section 40TU in\nrelation to the investigation.\n(2) The investigator:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TX\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) must identify the AFP practices issue in the report; and\n(b) may include in the report such recommendations as the\ninvestigator considers appropriate to address the AFP\npractices issue.\nSubdivision E—Dealing with AFP practices issues",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tw-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tw-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "84f5c45316789c13ac36c5fae8ef876296bd1e8cefcfb1c7d234e3742e0beaeb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40tw",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40TW AFP practices issue identified in course of dealing with AFP",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "conduct issue\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the investigator is satisfied that the information:\n(i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or\n(ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue;\nraises an AFP practices issue; and\n(b) the investigator prepares a report under section 40TU in\nrelation to the investigation.\n(2) The investigator:\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nDealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3\nSection 40TX\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(a) must identify the AFP practices issue in the report; and\n(b) may include in the report such recommendations as the\ninvestigator considers appropriate to address the AFP\npractices issue.\nSubdivision E—Dealing with AFP practices issues"
    },
    {
