    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40uc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40UC Division 3 investigation may be suspended pending outcome",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40uc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.127",
      "values:originalText": "of inquiry\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the Minister arranges under section 40UA for an inquiry to\nbe held into conduct or a matter; and\n(b) the conduct or matter is being dealt with, or is about to be\ndealt with, under Division 3.\n(2) The Commissioner may suspend further action in relation to the\nconduct or matter under Division 3 until the inquiry has been\ncompleted.\n(3) If the Commissioner:\n(a) receives a report in relation to the inquiry; and\n(b) is satisfied, having considered that report, that it is\nappropriate to do so;\nthe Commissioner may terminate the investigation of the conduct\nor matter under Division 3.\n(4) If the conduct or matter is being dealt with under Division 3 jointly\nby the Ombudsman and the Australian Federal Police, the\nCommissioner may take action under subsection (2) or (3) only\nafter consulting the Ombudsman.",
      "skos:definition": "of inquiry\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the Minister arranges under section 40UA for an inquiry to\nbe held into conduct or a matter; and\n(b) the conduct or matter is being dealt with, or is about to be\ndealt with, under Division 3.\n(2) The Commissioner may suspend further action in relation to the\nconduct or matter under Division 3 until the inquiry has been\ncompleted.\n(3) If the Commissioner:\n(a) receives a report in relation to the inquiry; and\n(b) is satisfied, having considered that report, that it is\nappropriate to do so;\nthe Commissioner may terminate the investigation of the conduct\nor matter under Division 3.\n(4) If the conduct or matter is being dealt with under Division 3 jointly\nby the Ombudsman and the Australian Federal Police, the\nCommissioner may take action under subsection (2) or (3) only\nafter consulting the Ombudsman.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40uc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40uc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40uc-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40uc-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "308866c88291da3b6cc37c779b83d5429c4967bcae3eb98c6c117b6c8909ddae"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40uc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40UC Division 3 investigation may be suspended pending outcome",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 127,
      "values:originalText": "of inquiry\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the Minister arranges under section 40UA for an inquiry to\nbe held into conduct or a matter; and\n(b) the conduct or matter is being dealt with, or is about to be\ndealt with, under Division 3.\n(2) The Commissioner may suspend further action in relation to the\nconduct or matter under Division 3 until the inquiry has been\ncompleted.\n(3) If the Commissioner:\n(a) receives a report in relation to the inquiry; and\n(b) is satisfied, having considered that report, that it is\nappropriate to do so;\nthe Commissioner may terminate the investigation of the conduct\nor matter under Division 3.\n(4) If the conduct or matter is being dealt with under Division 3 jointly\nby the Ombudsman and the Australian Federal Police, the\nCommissioner may take action under subsection (2) or (3) only\nafter consulting the Ombudsman."
    },
