      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.127",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the Commissioner:\n(a) receives a report in relation to the inquiry; and\n(b) is satisfied, having considered that report, that it is\nappropriate to do so;\nthe Commissioner may terminate the investigation of the conduct\nor matter under Division 3.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the Commissioner:\n(a) receives a report in relation to the inquiry; and\n(b) is satisfied, having considered that report, that it is\nappropriate to do so;\nthe Commissioner may terminate the investigation of the conduct\nor matter under Division 3.",
      "values:partOf": {
