    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40vb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40VB Manner of conducting investigation or inquiry",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40vb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The investigation or inquiry is to be conducted, subject to this\nDivision, in such manner as the investigator thinks fit.\n(2) If the Ombudsman makes an arrangement with the Commissioner\nunder section 8D of the Ombudsman Act 1976 in relation to the\ninvestigation of the issue, the investigator must:\n(a) investigate the issue jointly with the Ombudsman; and\n(b) investigate the issue in accordance with the arrangement.\n(3) If:\n(a) the investigator is investigating a category 3 conduct issue or\na corruption issue; and\n(b) the head of the unit constituted under section 40RD allocated\nthe issue to the investigator;\nthe head of that unit may give the investigator directions as to the\nmanner in which the investigation is to be conducted and the\ninvestigator must comply with those directions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The investigation or inquiry is to be conducted, subject to this\nDivision, in such manner as the investigator thinks fit.\n(2) If the Ombudsman makes an arrangement with the Commissioner\nunder section 8D of the Ombudsman Act 1976 in relation to the\ninvestigation of the issue, the investigator must:\n(a) investigate the issue jointly with the Ombudsman; and\n(b) investigate the issue in accordance with the arrangement.\n(3) If:\n(a) the investigator is investigating a category 3 conduct issue or\na corruption issue; and\n(b) the head of the unit constituted under section 40RD allocated\nthe issue to the investigator;\nthe head of that unit may give the investigator directions as to the\nmanner in which the investigation is to be conducted and the\ninvestigator must comply with those directions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40vb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40vb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40vb-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "66da0395439189a34388e3a004875add0e0354eebd1e9bc78e96784bf8f11833"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40vb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40VB Manner of conducting investigation or inquiry",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The investigation or inquiry is to be conducted, subject to this\nDivision, in such manner as the investigator thinks fit.\n(2) If the Ombudsman makes an arrangement with the Commissioner\nunder section 8D of the Ombudsman Act 1976 in relation to the\ninvestigation of the issue, the investigator must:\n(a) investigate the issue jointly with the Ombudsman; and\n(b) investigate the issue in accordance with the arrangement.\n(3) If:\n(a) the investigator is investigating a category 3 conduct issue or\na corruption issue; and\n(b) the head of the unit constituted under section 40RD allocated\nthe issue to the investigator;\nthe head of that unit may give the investigator directions as to the\nmanner in which the investigation is to be conducted and the\ninvestigator must comply with those directions."
    },
    {
