    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40vd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40VD Relationship with other laws",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40vd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.130",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 40VB and 40VC do not authorise an AFP appointee to\ncontravene, or fail to comply with, a law that would, if those\nsections had not been enacted, apply in relation to the investigation\nor inquiry.\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) affects the operation of any other\nprovision of this Division.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nInvestigative powers  Division 5\nSection 40VE\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 40VB and 40VC do not authorise an AFP appointee to\ncontravene, or fail to comply with, a law that would, if those\nsections had not been enacted, apply in relation to the investigation\nor inquiry.\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) affects the operation of any other\nprovision of this Division.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nInvestigative powers  Division 5\nSection 40VE\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
