    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40ve-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40VE(1) Directions to AFP appointee",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 131,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The investigator may, for the purposes of the investigation or\ninquiry, direct an AFP appointee:\n(a) to give the investigator information (in the manner and form\nspecified in the direction); or\n(b) to produce to the investigator a document, record or thing; or\n(c) to answer a question; or\n(d) to do anything else that is reasonably necessary for the\npurposes of obtaining evidence in relation to the investigation\nor inquiry.\nNote:\nFailure to comply with the direction is an offence against\nsubsection 40VH(1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must comply with direction.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Failure to comply is an offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Compliance is obligatory."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BEGINS",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Direction specifies when information must be provided.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Information is to be provided at some point in time.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The direction begins at a certain point in time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve-ss-1-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "IMPLIES",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Failure to comply implies an offence.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Compliance is necessary for the investigation.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Failure to comply implies an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40VE(2) Directions to AFP appointee",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40ve-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.131",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A direction under subsection (1) has no effect unless the\ninvestigator:\n(a) states in the direction that the AFP appointee to whom the\ndirection is given is being expressly directed under that\nsubsection; and\n(b) specifies in the direction the substance of the subject matter\nof the investigation or inquiry; and\n(c) if it is practicable to do so—gives the direction in writing;\nand\n(d) if the direction is given in writing—gives the AFP appointee\na copy of the direction.\nObligation to comply with direction",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A direction under subsection (1) has no effect unless the\ninvestigator:\n(a) states in the direction that the AFP appointee to whom the\ndirection is given is being expressly directed under that\nsubsection; and\n(b) specifies in the direction the substance of the subject matter\nof the investigation or inquiry; and\n(c) if it is practicable to do so—gives the direction in writing;\nand\n(d) if the direction is given in writing—gives the AFP appointee\na copy of the direction.\nObligation to comply with direction",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ve-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "375ab07cbc0aa747200950f563fdc31de6a758532a710331483adfaa758cc621",
      "skos:note": "Investigator must state direction, specify investigation subject matter, and provide written copy to AFP appointee.",
      "dc:description": "[]"
    },
    {
