    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40wa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40WA Record keeping",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40wa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.138",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner must ensure that adequate records are kept for\nthe purposes of this Part.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner must ensure\nthat records are kept of:\n(a) information that is given under section 40SA; and\n(b) the action (if any) that is taken in relation to the AFP conduct\nor practices issue raised by that information; and\n(c) if the issue is an AFP conduct issue—the action (if any) that\nis taken in relation to any AFP practices issue that is:\n(i) brought, under section 40TK, to the attention of an AFP\nappointee; or\n(ii) identified, under section 40TW, in a report prepared\nunder section 40TU;\nas a result of the AFP conduct issue being dealt with under\nthis Part.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if subsection 40SC(2) (which deals\nwith category 1 conduct issues that are resolved without being\nrecorded) applies to the information.\n(4) The National Anti-Corruption Commissioner is entitled to have\naccess to the records kept under this section for the purposes of\nperforming the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner’s\nfunctions.\n(5) Without limiting section 40XC, the Ombudsman is entitled to have\naccess to the records kept under this section for the purposes of\nperforming the Ombudsman’s functions.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nRecord keeping  Division 6\nSection 40WB\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner must ensure that adequate records are kept for\nthe purposes of this Part.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner must ensure\nthat records are kept of:\n(a) information that is given under section 40SA; and\n(b) the action (if any) that is taken in relation to the AFP conduct\nor practices issue raised by that information; and\n(c) if the issue is an AFP conduct issue—the action (if any) that\nis taken in relation to any AFP practices issue that is:\n(i) brought, under section 40TK, to the attention of an AFP\nappointee; or\n(ii) identified, under section 40TW, in a report prepared\nunder section 40TU;\nas a result of the AFP conduct issue being dealt with under\nthis Part.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if subsection 40SC(2) (which deals\nwith category 1 conduct issues that are resolved without being\nrecorded) applies to the information.\n(4) The National Anti-Corruption Commissioner is entitled to have\naccess to the records kept under this section for the purposes of\nperforming the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner’s\nfunctions.\n(5) Without limiting section 40XC, the Ombudsman is entitled to have\naccess to the records kept under this section for the purposes of\nperforming the Ombudsman’s functions.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nRecord keeping  Division 6\nSection 40WB\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40wa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40wa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40wa-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40wa-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40wa-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c02ccaa5c1405ea4cb6426d9007cf99f6fdae3ac059fc8a855e1f7c18c38395b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40wa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40WA Record keeping",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 138,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner must ensure that adequate records are kept for\nthe purposes of this Part.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner must ensure\nthat records are kept of:\n(a) information that is given under section 40SA; and\n(b) the action (if any) that is taken in relation to the AFP conduct\nor practices issue raised by that information; and\n(c) if the issue is an AFP conduct issue—the action (if any) that\nis taken in relation to any AFP practices issue that is:\n(i) brought, under section 40TK, to the attention of an AFP\nappointee; or\n(ii) identified, under section 40TW, in a report prepared\nunder section 40TU;\nas a result of the AFP conduct issue being dealt with under\nthis Part.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if subsection 40SC(2) (which deals\nwith category 1 conduct issues that are resolved without being\nrecorded) applies to the information.\n(4) The National Anti-Corruption Commissioner is entitled to have\naccess to the records kept under this section for the purposes of\nperforming the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner’s\nfunctions.\n(5) Without limiting section 40XC, the Ombudsman is entitled to have\naccess to the records kept under this section for the purposes of\nperforming the Ombudsman’s functions.\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nRecord keeping  Division 6\nSection 40WB\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025"
    },
