    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40xa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40XA Annual reviews by Ombudsman",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40xa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.140",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the review periods are:\n(a) the period of 12 months commencing on the day on which\nthe Law Enforcement (AFP Professional Standards and\nRelated Measures) Act 2006 commences; and\n(b) each succeeding period of 12 months.\n(2) At least once in each review period, the Ombudsman must, for the\npurposes of reviewing the administration of this Part during that\nperiod, inspect the records of AFP conduct issues and AFP\npractices issues that have been, or are being, dealt with under\nDivisions 3 and 4 during that period.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the review periods are:\n(a) the period of 12 months commencing on the day on which\nthe Law Enforcement (AFP Professional Standards and\nRelated Measures) Act 2006 commences; and\n(b) each succeeding period of 12 months.\n(2) At least once in each review period, the Ombudsman must, for the\npurposes of reviewing the administration of this Part during that\nperiod, inspect the records of AFP conduct issues and AFP\npractices issues that have been, or are being, dealt with under\nDivisions 3 and 4 during that period.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40xa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40xa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "08a47a984f1a016011622435335ba866c478e3c8cf0f5b5b6bb64cd2cd99f8f1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40xa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40XA Annual reviews by Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 140,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the review periods are:\n(a) the period of 12 months commencing on the day on which\nthe Law Enforcement (AFP Professional Standards and\nRelated Measures) Act 2006 commences; and\n(b) each succeeding period of 12 months.\n(2) At least once in each review period, the Ombudsman must, for the\npurposes of reviewing the administration of this Part during that\nperiod, inspect the records of AFP conduct issues and AFP\npractices issues that have been, or are being, dealt with under\nDivisions 3 and 4 during that period."
    },
