    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40xd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40XD Annual reports by Ombudsman",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40xd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.140",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman must, as soon as practicable after 30 June each\nyear, prepare a report of the Ombudsman’s work and activities\nunder this Division during the preceding 12 months and give\ncopies of the report to the President of the Senate and the Speaker\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nOmbudsman review  Division 7\nSection 40XD\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nof the House of Representatives for presentation to the Senate and\nthe House of Representatives, respectively.\n(2) The report must include comments as to the comprehensiveness\nand adequacy of the administration of matters under Divisions 3\nand 4.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Ombudsman must, as soon as practicable after 30 June each\nyear, prepare a report of the Ombudsman’s work and activities\nunder this Division during the preceding 12 months and give\ncopies of the report to the President of the Senate and the Speaker\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nOmbudsman review  Division 7\nSection 40XD\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nof the House of Representatives for presentation to the Senate and\nthe House of Representatives, respectively.\n(2) The report must include comments as to the comprehensiveness\nand adequacy of the administration of matters under Divisions 3\nand 4.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40xd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40xd-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4769b7c74b92a7d64f135b3149c10481898d2d8036687a9f5f0e3fed19dcff43"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40xd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40XD Annual reports by Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 140,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman must, as soon as practicable after 30 June each\nyear, prepare a report of the Ombudsman’s work and activities\nunder this Division during the preceding 12 months and give\ncopies of the report to the President of the Senate and the Speaker\n\n\nProfessional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V\nOmbudsman review  Division 7\nSection 40XD\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nof the House of Representatives for presentation to the Senate and\nthe House of Representatives, respectively.\n(2) The report must include comments as to the comprehensiveness\nand adequacy of the administration of matters under Divisions 3\nand 4."
    },
