    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ya",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40YA Victimisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40ya"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.142",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if the person causes, or threatens to\ncause, detriment to another person (the victim) on the ground that\nthe victim, or any other person:\n(a) has given, or may give, information under this Part; or\n(b) has produced, or may produce, a document, record or thing to\na person under this Part.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a threat may be:\n(a) express or implied; or\n(b) conditional or unconditional.\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against subsection (1), it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person threatened actually feared that\nthe threat would be carried out.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if the person causes, or threatens to\ncause, detriment to another person (the victim) on the ground that\nthe victim, or any other person:\n(a) has given, or may give, information under this Part; or\n(b) has produced, or may produce, a document, record or thing to\na person under this Part.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a threat may be:\n(a) express or implied; or\n(b) conditional or unconditional.\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against subsection (1), it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person threatened actually feared that\nthe threat would be carried out.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ya-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ya-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ya-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "715f4677025f3730228c6d617bcde49adf6a268725f9bee301b54e0e4605e0dd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-40ya",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40YA Victimisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 142,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if the person causes, or threatens to\ncause, detriment to another person (the victim) on the ground that\nthe victim, or any other person:\n(a) has given, or may give, information under this Part; or\n(b) has produced, or may produce, a document, record or thing to\na person under this Part.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a threat may be:\n(a) express or implied; or\n(b) conditional or unconditional.\n(3) In a prosecution for an offence against subsection (1), it is not\nnecessary to prove that the person threatened actually feared that\nthe threat would be carried out."
    },
