    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42F(2) Effective control of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-42f-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting the generality of any other provision of this Part,\nin determining:\n(a) whether or not property is subject to the effective control of a\nperson; or\n(b) whether or not there are reasonable grounds to believe that\nproperty is subject to the effective control of a person;\nregard may be had to:\n(c) shareholdings in, debentures over or directorships of a\ncompany that has an interest (whether direct or indirect) in\nthe property; and\n(d) a trust that has a relationship to the property; and\n(e) family, domestic and business relationships between persons\nhaving an interest in the property, or in companies of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph (c) or trusts of the kind mentioned in\nparagraph (d), and other persons.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting the generality of any other provision of this Part,\nin determining:\n(a) whether or not property is subject to the effective control of a\nperson; or\n(b) whether or not there are reasonable grounds to believe that\nproperty is subject to the effective control of a person;\nregard may be had to:\n(c) shareholdings in, debentures over or directorships of a\ncompany that has an interest (whether direct or indirect) in\nthe property; and\n(d) a trust that has a relationship to the property; and\n(e) family, domestic and business relationships between persons\nhaving an interest in the property, or in companies of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph (c) or trusts of the kind mentioned in\nparagraph (d), and other persons.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "13056226da59f33f7c87016be9d6576edae551db0da8216b1c9a4cf12530de91",
      "skos:note": "Determine whether property is subject to effective control of a person",
      "dc:description": "Reasonable grounds to believe property is subject to effective control"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-42f-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42F(2) Effective control of property",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting the generality of any other provision of this Part,\nin determining:\n(a) whether or not property is subject to the effective control of a\nperson; or\n(b) whether or not there are reasonable grounds to believe that\nproperty is subject to the effective control of a person;\nregard may be had to:\n(c) shareholdings in, debentures over or directorships of a\ncompany that has an interest (whether direct or indirect) in\nthe property; and\n(d) a trust that has a relationship to the property; and\n(e) family, domestic and business relationships between persons\nhaving an interest in the property, or in companies of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph (c) or trusts of the kind mentioned in\nparagraph (d), and other persons."
    },
