    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42F(3) Effective control of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-42f-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(e), family relationships are taken\nto include the following (without limitation):\n(a) relationships between de facto partners (within the meaning\nof the Acts Interpretation Act 1901);\n(b) relationships of child and parent that arise if someone is the\nchild of a person because of the definition of child in this\nsection;\n(c) relationships traced through relationships mentioned in\nparagraphs (a) and (b).",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(e), family relationships are taken\nto include the following (without limitation):\n(a) relationships between de facto partners (within the meaning\nof the Acts Interpretation Act 1901);\n(b) relationships of child and parent that arise if someone is the\nchild of a person because of the definition of child in this\nsection;\n(c) relationships traced through relationships mentioned in\nparagraphs (a) and (b).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f655828e0d5951b8af7fa88413a9ba19970ffaeea89bf70bce29ae6d9c760cdb",
      "skos:note": "Defines family relationships for the purpose of paragraph (2)(e)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-42f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42F(3) Effective control of property",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(e), family relationships are taken\nto include the following (without limitation):\n(a) relationships between de facto partners (within the meaning\nof the Acts Interpretation Act 1901);\n(b) relationships of child and parent that arise if someone is the\nchild of a person because of the definition of child in this\nsection;\n(c) relationships traced through relationships mentioned in\nparagraphs (a) and (b)."
    },
