    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42F(4) Effective control of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-42f-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In this section:\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nIntroductory  Division 1\nSection 42G\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nchild: without limiting who is a child of a person for the purposes\nof this Act, someone is the child of a person if he or she is a child\nof the person within the meaning of the Family Law Act 1975.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In this section:\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nIntroductory  Division 1\nSection 42G\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nchild: without limiting who is a child of a person for the purposes\nof this Act, someone is the child of a person if he or she is a child\nof the person within the meaning of the Family Law Act 1975.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-42f-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f7863757c7396862c23305aae644ffbce31ac533f559cdda1b774929405d2e3d",
      "skos:note": "Defines who is considered a child for the purposes of the Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-42f-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42F(4) Effective control of property",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In this section:\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nIntroductory  Division 1\nSection 42G\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nchild: without limiting who is a child of a person for the purposes\nof this Act, someone is the child of a person if he or she is a child\nof the person within the meaning of the Family Law Act 1975."
    },
