    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45A(2) Application for superannuation order: evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-45a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In an application for a superannuation order, any finding of fact\nmade by a court in any proceedings for the offence to which the\napplication relates, is prima facie evidence of that fact and the\nfinding may be proved by the production of documents, under the\nseal of the court, in which the finding appears.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In an application for a superannuation order, any finding of fact\nmade by a court in any proceedings for the offence to which the\napplication relates, is prima facie evidence of that fact and the\nfinding may be proved by the production of documents, under the\nseal of the court, in which the finding appears.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b918ea2ccdb05947d4b4dc1d2ce542e7cd51f12a40fab53a2c1439fa9d257613",
      "skos:note": "Prima facie evidence of fact in proceedings"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-45a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45A(2) Application for superannuation order: evidence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In an application for a superannuation order, any finding of fact\nmade by a court in any proceedings for the offence to which the\napplication relates, is prima facie evidence of that fact and the\nfinding may be proved by the production of documents, under the\nseal of the court, in which the finding appears."
    },
