      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "holds",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Employer contributions or benefits are held in a specified fund",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) stating that employer contributions or benefits made or payable by the Commonwealth...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "is prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the certificate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a-ss-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "holds",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Employer contributions or benefits are equal to the sum of those contributions or benefits as at the specified day plus the amount of interest accrued under the scheme",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) stating the amount that equals the sum of those contributions or benefits...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "is prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the certificate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45A(4) Application for superannuation order: evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-45a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In an application for a superannuation order in respect of the\nperson, a certificate signed or sealed by the person’s\nsuperannuation authority:\n(a) stating that benefits have been paid to the person under the\nrelevant superannuation scheme; and\n(b) stating the amount that equals the sum of the benefits so paid\nas at the specified day; and\n(c) stating another amount that equals the part of the amount\nmentioned in paragraph (b) that is attributable to the sum of\nthe employee contributions paid under the scheme by the\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nLoss of superannuation: corruption offences  Division 2\nSection 46\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nperson as at the specified day plus the amount of interest on\nthose contributions accrued under the scheme before that\nday;\nis prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the certificate.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In an application for a superannuation order in respect of the\nperson, a certificate signed or sealed by the person’s\nsuperannuation authority:\n(a) stating that benefits have been paid to the person under the\nrelevant superannuation scheme; and\n(b) stating the amount that equals the sum of the benefits so paid\nas at the specified day; and\n(c) stating another amount that equals the part of the amount\nmentioned in paragraph (b) that is attributable to the sum of\nthe employee contributions paid under the scheme by the\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nLoss of superannuation: corruption offences  Division 2\nSection 46\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nperson as at the specified day plus the amount of interest on\nthose contributions accrued under the scheme before that\nday;\nis prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the certificate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-45a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20b428cc4663fd498e48b07d7f02f16e0d424b7df4abbddc96935a3b1e4b8e2e",
      "skos:note": "A certificate signed or sealed by the person’s superannuation authority is required as evidence for an application for a superannuation order.",
      "dc:description": "The certificate must state that benefits have been paid to the person under the relevant superannuation scheme, and the amount of those benefits as at the specified day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-45a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45A(4) Application for superannuation order: evidence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In an application for a superannuation order in respect of the\nperson, a certificate signed or sealed by the person’s\nsuperannuation authority:\n(a) stating that benefits have been paid to the person under the\nrelevant superannuation scheme; and\n(b) stating the amount that equals the sum of the benefits so paid\nas at the specified day; and\n(c) stating another amount that equals the part of the amount\nmentioned in paragraph (b) that is attributable to the sum of\nthe employee contributions paid under the scheme by the\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nLoss of superannuation: corruption offences  Division 2\nSection 46\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nperson as at the specified day plus the amount of interest on\nthose contributions accrued under the scheme before that\nday;\nis prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the certificate."
    },
