    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-47-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47(3) Effect of superannuation order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-47-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.162",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Despite the Superannuation Act, or any other Act or any\nagreement, where subsection (1) applies to a person:\n(a) who:\n(i) was an AFP employee at the time the relevant\ncorruption offence was committed but was not such an\nemployee when charged with that offence; or\n(ii) was an old law member or staff member at the time the\nrelevant corruption offence was committed but was not\nsuch a member or an AFP employee when charged with\nthat offence; and\n(b) who would, but for that subsection, have been entitled to\npayment of benefits under the relevant superannuation\nscheme on or after the day on which the superannuation order\ntakes effect;\nthe person is entitled, on the day on which he or she ceases to be a\nmember of the scheme, to payment of an amount worked out using\nthe formula:\nwhere:\nAC is an amount equal to the sum of the employee contributions\npaid under the scheme by the person plus the amount of interest on\nthose contributions accrued under the scheme; and\nAC – AR",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Despite the Superannuation Act, or any other Act or any\nagreement, where subsection (1) applies to a person:\n(a) who:\n(i) was an AFP employee at the time the relevant\ncorruption offence was committed but was not such an\nemployee when charged with that offence; or\n(ii) was an old law member or staff member at the time the\nrelevant corruption offence was committed but was not\nsuch a member or an AFP employee when charged with\nthat offence; and\n(b) who would, but for that subsection, have been entitled to\npayment of benefits under the relevant superannuation\nscheme on or after the day on which the superannuation order\ntakes effect;\nthe person is entitled, on the day on which he or she ceases to be a\nmember of the scheme, to payment of an amount worked out using\nthe formula:\nwhere:\nAC is an amount equal to the sum of the employee contributions\npaid under the scheme by the person plus the amount of interest on\nthose contributions accrued under the scheme; and\nAC – AR",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-47"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-47-ss-3-norm"
        },
