      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f6b3a0957ca43393000f4f56897247458460658e0a755b23e321691eb8bba4f6",
      "skos:note": "Variation of superannuation order by DPP after its effect"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-47a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47A(1) Superannuation orders: variation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a superannuation order made in respect of a person:\n(a) specifies an amount under subsection 46(3) or (4); and\n(b) takes effect on a day that is later than the day on which the\norder is made;\nthe DPP may, as soon as practicable after the order takes effect,\napply to the court that made the order to vary the order by\nsubstituting for the specified amount an increased amount, having\nregard to any amount of employer contributions or benefits paid by\nthe Commonwealth or a Commonwealth organisation in respect of\nthe person during the prescribed period."
    },
