          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-47b-ss-3-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-47b-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-47b-ss-3-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "896d85c8796ff7ef809ece3f08fd6d7e8acaa7a78497e0cfd4ad196a6c86ce8c",
      "skos:note": "Payable amount for revocation of superannuation order",
      "dc:description": "Amount determined by the Finance Minister"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-47b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47B(3) Superannuation orders: revocation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where:\n(a) a superannuation order is made in relation to a person who is\ntaken to be convicted because of paragraph 42C(1)(b); and\n(b) the superannuation order is to be taken to have been revoked;\nthere is payable to the person an amount determined by the Finance\nMinister, being an amount that the Minister administering the\nCrimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989 considers to be a fair\nrecompense to the person, having regard to:\n(c) any amount paid to the person under subsection 47(2) or (3);\nand\n(d) any amount recovered from the person under a recovery\norder against the person; and\n(e) any other financial loss sustained by the person as a result of\nthe superannuation order; and\n(f) any other matters that the Minister administering the Crimes\n(Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989 thinks are relevant in the\ncircumstances of the case."
    },
