    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49A(1) Application for restraining order",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 166,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a person (in this Division called the defendant):\n(a) has been convicted of an offence; or\n(b) has been, or is about to be, charged with an offence;\nthe DPP may apply to the appropriate court for a restraining order\nagainst specified property of the defendant or of another person, or\nboth."
    },
