    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49b-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49B(6) Making of restraining orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49b-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.166",
      "values:originalText": "(6) A court may refuse to make a restraining order if the\nCommonwealth refuses or fails to give the court such undertakings\nas the court considers appropriate with respect to the payment of\ndamages or costs, or both, in relation to the making and operation\nof the order.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) A court may refuse to make a restraining order if the\nCommonwealth refuses or fails to give the court such undertakings\nas the court considers appropriate with respect to the payment of\ndamages or costs, or both, in relation to the making and operation\nof the order.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49b-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49b-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee017d19c0e6a8e8eb33b1423553c36b0571e20b1148f2dd866174ad00c7254a",
      "skos:note": "Court refusal to make restraining order based on Commonwealth's undertakings"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49b-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49B(6) Making of restraining orders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 166,
      "values:originalText": "(6) A court may refuse to make a restraining order if the\nCommonwealth refuses or fails to give the court such undertakings\nas the court considers appropriate with respect to the payment of\ndamages or costs, or both, in relation to the making and operation\nof the order."
    },
