      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49c-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Establishes obligations for a restraining order",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49D Affidavit of police officer needed in certain cases",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where an application is made for a restraining order and the\ndefendant has not been convicted of the offence concerned, the\ncourt must not make a restraining order unless:\n(a) the application for the order is supported by an affidavit of a\npolice officer stating that the officer believes the defendant\ncommitted the offence; and\n(b) the court is satisfied, having regard to the matters contained\nin the affidavit, that there are reasonable grounds for so\nbelieving.\n(2) Where an application for a restraining order is made against\nspecified property of a person other than the defendant, the court\nmust not make a restraining order against the property unless:\n(a) the application is supported by an affidavit of a police officer\nstating that the officer believes that the property is subject to\nthe effective control of the defendant; and\n(b) the court is satisfied, having regard to the matters contained\nin the affidavit, that there are reasonable grounds for so\nbelieving.\n(3) An affidavit made by a police officer for the purpose of this section\nstating that the officer believes a particular matter must set out the\ngrounds on which the officer holds that belief.\n(4) The court may, at any time before the final determination of an\napplication for:\n(a) a restraining order; or\n(b) an extension of the period of effect of a restraining order;\ndirect the DPP to give or publish notice of the application to a\nspecified person or class of persons in the manner and within the\ntime the court thinks appropriate.\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49E\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(5) In this section:\npolice officer means a member of the Australian Federal Police or\nof the police force of a State or Territory.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where an application is made for a restraining order and the\ndefendant has not been convicted of the offence concerned, the\ncourt must not make a restraining order unless:\n(a) the application for the order is supported by an affidavit of a\npolice officer stating that the officer believes the defendant\ncommitted the offence; and\n(b) the court is satisfied, having regard to the matters contained\nin the affidavit, that there are reasonable grounds for so\nbelieving.\n(2) Where an application for a restraining order is made against\nspecified property of a person other than the defendant, the court\nmust not make a restraining order against the property unless:\n(a) the application is supported by an affidavit of a police officer\nstating that the officer believes that the property is subject to\nthe effective control of the defendant; and\n(b) the court is satisfied, having regard to the matters contained\nin the affidavit, that there are reasonable grounds for so\nbelieving.\n(3) An affidavit made by a police officer for the purpose of this section\nstating that the officer believes a particular matter must set out the\ngrounds on which the officer holds that belief.\n(4) The court may, at any time before the final determination of an\napplication for:\n(a) a restraining order; or\n(b) an extension of the period of effect of a restraining order;\ndirect the DPP to give or publish notice of the application to a\nspecified person or class of persons in the manner and within the\ntime the court thinks appropriate.\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49E\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(5) In this section:\npolice officer means a member of the Australian Federal Police or\nof the police force of a State or Territory.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49d-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49d-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f8990a421c1b101ef2da9173066fc0e585450208161a96f626189b6634c4292a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49D Affidavit of police officer needed in certain cases",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where an application is made for a restraining order and the\ndefendant has not been convicted of the offence concerned, the\ncourt must not make a restraining order unless:\n(a) the application for the order is supported by an affidavit of a\npolice officer stating that the officer believes the defendant\ncommitted the offence; and\n(b) the court is satisfied, having regard to the matters contained\nin the affidavit, that there are reasonable grounds for so\nbelieving.\n(2) Where an application for a restraining order is made against\nspecified property of a person other than the defendant, the court\nmust not make a restraining order against the property unless:\n(a) the application is supported by an affidavit of a police officer\nstating that the officer believes that the property is subject to\nthe effective control of the defendant; and\n(b) the court is satisfied, having regard to the matters contained\nin the affidavit, that there are reasonable grounds for so\nbelieving.\n(3) An affidavit made by a police officer for the purpose of this section\nstating that the officer believes a particular matter must set out the\ngrounds on which the officer holds that belief.\n(4) The court may, at any time before the final determination of an\napplication for:\n(a) a restraining order; or\n(b) an extension of the period of effect of a restraining order;\ndirect the DPP to give or publish notice of the application to a\nspecified person or class of persons in the manner and within the\ntime the court thinks appropriate.\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49E\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(5) In this section:\npolice officer means a member of the Australian Federal Police or\nof the police force of a State or Territory."
    },
