    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49ea",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49EA Extension of certain restraining orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49ea"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.169",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application made by\nthe DPP before the end of the period mentioned in\nsubsection 49E(2), extend the period of operation of a restraining\norder made in reliance on that subsection.\n(2) Subsections 49D(1), (2), (3) and (5) apply, with the necessary\nchanges made, to the extension of the period of operation of a\nrestraining order made in reliance on subsection 49E(2) in the same\nway as they apply to the making of a restraining order.\n(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection (1) for the extension of a restraining order to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may\nhave an interest in the property.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application made by\nthe DPP before the end of the period mentioned in\nsubsection 49E(2), extend the period of operation of a restraining\norder made in reliance on that subsection.\n(2) Subsections 49D(1), (2), (3) and (5) apply, with the necessary\nchanges made, to the extension of the period of operation of a\nrestraining order made in reliance on subsection 49E(2) in the same\nway as they apply to the making of a restraining order.\n(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection (1) for the extension of a restraining order to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may\nhave an interest in the property.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49ea-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49ea-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49ea-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cebbea2050e5bf4811ed4786beafd251b56ec9ce23a02b23f6e3cb6da818c9ad"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49ea",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49EA Extension of certain restraining orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 169,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application made by\nthe DPP before the end of the period mentioned in\nsubsection 49E(2), extend the period of operation of a restraining\norder made in reliance on that subsection.\n(2) Subsections 49D(1), (2), (3) and (5) apply, with the necessary\nchanges made, to the extension of the period of operation of a\nrestraining order made in reliance on subsection 49E(2) in the same\nway as they apply to the making of a restraining order.\n(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection (1) for the extension of a restraining order to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may\nhave an interest in the property."
    },
