    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49L Registration of restraining orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n(a) a restraining order applies to property of a particular kind;\nand\n(b) the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State\nor Territory provide for the registration of title to, or charges\nover, property of that kind;\nthe authority responsible for administering those provisions may,\non application by the DPP, record on the register kept under those\nprovisions particulars of the restraining order.\n(2) Where particulars of a restraining order are recorded under\nsubsection (1), a person who later deals with the property is to be\ntaken, for the purposes of section 49M, to have notice of the\nrestraining order at the time of the dealing.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where:\n(a) a restraining order applies to property of a particular kind;\nand\n(b) the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State\nor Territory provide for the registration of title to, or charges\nover, property of that kind;\nthe authority responsible for administering those provisions may,\non application by the DPP, record on the register kept under those\nprovisions particulars of the restraining order.\n(2) Where particulars of a restraining order are recorded under\nsubsection (1), a person who later deals with the property is to be\ntaken, for the purposes of section 49M, to have notice of the\nrestraining order at the time of the dealing.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49l-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "308ddaa5df0f43941bf97c07410728d1f60cdf5f65ea22070f5a5371341aac71"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49L Registration of restraining orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n(a) a restraining order applies to property of a particular kind;\nand\n(b) the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State\nor Territory provide for the registration of title to, or charges\nover, property of that kind;\nthe authority responsible for administering those provisions may,\non application by the DPP, record on the register kept under those\nprovisions particulars of the restraining order.\n(2) Where particulars of a restraining order are recorded under\nsubsection (1), a person who later deals with the property is to be\ntaken, for the purposes of section 49M, to have notice of the\nrestraining order at the time of the dealing."
    },
