        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who intentionally contravenes a restraining order by\ndisposing of, or otherwise dealing with, property that is subject to\nthe restraining order commits an offence punishable, upon\nconviction, by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 5 years.\n(2) Where:\n(a) a restraining order is made against property; and\n(b) the property is disposed of, or otherwise dealt with, in\ncontravention of the restraining order; and\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49N\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(c) the disposition or dealing was either not for sufficient\nconsideration or not in favour of a person who acted in good\nfaith;\nthe DPP may apply to the court that made the restraining order for\nan order that the disposition or dealing be set aside.\n(3) Where the DPP makes an application under subsection (2) in\nrelation to a disposition or dealing, the court may make an order:\n(a) setting the disposition or dealing aside as from the day on\nwhich it took place; or\n(b) setting the disposition or dealing aside as from the day of the\norder under this subsection and declaring the respective\nrights of any persons who acquired interests in the property\non or after the day on which the disposition or dealing took\nplace and before the day of the order under this subsection.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person who intentionally contravenes a restraining order by\ndisposing of, or otherwise dealing with, property that is subject to\nthe restraining order commits an offence punishable, upon\nconviction, by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 5 years.\n(2) Where:\n(a) a restraining order is made against property; and\n(b) the property is disposed of, or otherwise dealt with, in\ncontravention of the restraining order; and\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49N\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(c) the disposition or dealing was either not for sufficient\nconsideration or not in favour of a person who acted in good\nfaith;\nthe DPP may apply to the court that made the restraining order for\nan order that the disposition or dealing be set aside.\n(3) Where the DPP makes an application under subsection (2) in\nrelation to a disposition or dealing, the court may make an order:\n(a) setting the disposition or dealing aside as from the day on\nwhich it took place; or\n(b) setting the disposition or dealing aside as from the day of the\norder under this subsection and declaring the respective\nrights of any persons who acquired interests in the property\non or after the day on which the disposition or dealing took\nplace and before the day of the order under this subsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49m-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49m-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "edb03f01a84bb40160f6c037b6cdfdb019ba0527811a2b0883fe925780f4f614"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49M Contravention of restraining orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who intentionally contravenes a restraining order by\ndisposing of, or otherwise dealing with, property that is subject to\nthe restraining order commits an offence punishable, upon\nconviction, by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 5 years.\n(2) Where:\n(a) a restraining order is made against property; and\n(b) the property is disposed of, or otherwise dealt with, in\ncontravention of the restraining order; and\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49N\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\n(c) the disposition or dealing was either not for sufficient\nconsideration or not in favour of a person who acted in good\nfaith;\nthe DPP may apply to the court that made the restraining order for\nan order that the disposition or dealing be set aside.\n(3) Where the DPP makes an application under subsection (2) in\nrelation to a disposition or dealing, the court may make an order:\n(a) setting the disposition or dealing aside as from the day on\nwhich it took place; or\n(b) setting the disposition or dealing aside as from the day of the\norder under this subsection and declaring the respective\nrights of any persons who acquired interests in the property\non or after the day on which the disposition or dealing took\nplace and before the day of the order under this subsection."
    },
