    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49Q Extension of period of effect of restraining orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.176",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The DPP may, before the end of the relevant period in relation to a\nrestraining order made in reliance on a person’s conviction of an\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49R\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\noffence or the charging, or proposed charging, of a person with an\noffence, apply to the court that made the restraining order for an\nextension of the period of effect of the order.\n(2) Where, on an application for an extension of the period of effect of\na restraining order, the court is satisfied:\n(a) that a recovery order has been, or may still be, made against\nthe person; and\n(b) where the property concerned is the property of another\nperson—an order under subsection 53A(1) has been, or may\nstill be, made;\nthe court may:\n(c) by order, extend the period of effect of the restraining order;\nand\n(d) make such other order or orders as it thinks appropriate in\nrelation to the operation of the restraining order.\n(3) The DPP must give a person written notice of an application in\nrelation to a restraining order in respect of the person’s property.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The DPP may, before the end of the relevant period in relation to a\nrestraining order made in reliance on a person’s conviction of an\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49R\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\noffence or the charging, or proposed charging, of a person with an\noffence, apply to the court that made the restraining order for an\nextension of the period of effect of the order.\n(2) Where, on an application for an extension of the period of effect of\na restraining order, the court is satisfied:\n(a) that a recovery order has been, or may still be, made against\nthe person; and\n(b) where the property concerned is the property of another\nperson—an order under subsection 53A(1) has been, or may\nstill be, made;\nthe court may:\n(c) by order, extend the period of effect of the restraining order;\nand\n(d) make such other order or orders as it thinks appropriate in\nrelation to the operation of the restraining order.\n(3) The DPP must give a person written notice of an application in\nrelation to a restraining order in respect of the person’s property.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-49q-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "62ec5179c56b307be560606e7e9e77ef4d5d4fb55bab740f6d0b2de80ffae876"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-49q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49Q Extension of period of effect of restraining orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 176,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The DPP may, before the end of the relevant period in relation to a\nrestraining order made in reliance on a person’s conviction of an\n\n\nLoss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA\nRestraining orders  Division 3A\nSection 49R\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\noffence or the charging, or proposed charging, of a person with an\noffence, apply to the court that made the restraining order for an\nextension of the period of effect of the order.\n(2) Where, on an application for an extension of the period of effect of\na restraining order, the court is satisfied:\n(a) that a recovery order has been, or may still be, made against\nthe person; and\n(b) where the property concerned is the property of another\nperson—an order under subsection 53A(1) has been, or may\nstill be, made;\nthe court may:\n(c) by order, extend the period of effect of the restraining order;\nand\n(d) make such other order or orders as it thinks appropriate in\nrelation to the operation of the restraining order.\n(3) The DPP must give a person written notice of an application in\nrelation to a restraining order in respect of the person’s property."
    },
