      "cml:integrityHash": "209f6c0a09cc4fd5f86a72f21816ec3093b066b3bfc52e2114603f9337a89a2e",
      "skos:note": "Property subject to effective control of a person may be declared available for recovery order satisfaction. Suspension of superannuation rights upon charging with corruption offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-51-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51(1) Person ceases to be an AFP employee: persons charged with",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n(a) a person is charged with an offence;\n(b) the person ceases, for any reason, to be an AFP employee on\nor after the day on which the person is charged (whether\nbecause the period of the person’s engagement ends, by\noperation of law or because of anything done by the person\nor the Commissioner);\nthen, if the Commissioner believes on reasonable grounds that the\noffence is a corruption offence, the Commissioner shall notify the\nperson’s superannuation authority in writing that the person’s\nrights and entitlements under the relevant superannuation scheme\nare suspended."
    },
