        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc7351de02edd16fcfbb6a78be93b991470d7e2a7752679d34d170dd74fbfc08",
      "skos:note": "Property subject to effective control of a person may be declared available for recovery order satisfaction. Suspension of superannuation rights upon charging with corruption offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-51-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51(1) Person ceases to be an AFP employee: persons charged with",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where an appropriate court makes a recovery order against a\nperson, it may, on application by the DPP, if it thinks that\nparticular property is subject to the effective control of the person,\nmake an order declaring that the whole, or a specified part, of that\nproperty is available to satisfy the recovery order."
    },
