    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-61",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61 Awards for bravery etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-61"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.185",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where an AFP appointee has, by his or her bravery or other\nconspicuous conduct or by his or her diligent service, merited a\nprescribed award, the Commissioner may confer the award on that\nperson.\n(1A) If the Commissioner is satisfied that a person (other than an AFP\nappointee) has, by his or her bravery, or other conspicuous\nconduct, in assisting the Australian Federal Police, merited a\nprescribed award, the Commissioner may confer the award on that\nperson.\n(2) An award shall be conferred on the basis of such criteria as are\nprescribed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where an AFP appointee has, by his or her bravery or other\nconspicuous conduct or by his or her diligent service, merited a\nprescribed award, the Commissioner may confer the award on that\nperson.\n(1A) If the Commissioner is satisfied that a person (other than an AFP\nappointee) has, by his or her bravery, or other conspicuous\nconduct, in assisting the Australian Federal Police, merited a\nprescribed award, the Commissioner may confer the award on that\nperson.\n(2) An award shall be conferred on the basis of such criteria as are\nprescribed.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-61-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-61-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-61-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9daca4290d7ee0110b4c06799e130500a64ca1050b087e7a160b1083c8d1955e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-61",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "61 Awards for bravery etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 185,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where an AFP appointee has, by his or her bravery or other\nconspicuous conduct or by his or her diligent service, merited a\nprescribed award, the Commissioner may confer the award on that\nperson.\n(1A) If the Commissioner is satisfied that a person (other than an AFP\nappointee) has, by his or her bravery, or other conspicuous\nconduct, in assisting the Australian Federal Police, merited a\nprescribed award, the Commissioner may confer the award on that\nperson.\n(2) An award shall be conferred on the basis of such criteria as are\nprescribed."
    },
