      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.185",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if the person dishonestly represents\nthat a police award has been conferred on the person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\nPolice award\n(2) For the purposes of this section, a police award is an award,\ncommendation, citation, medal or other decoration (however\ndescribed) that has been or may be conferred on the Commissioner\nor an AFP appointee for police services that are provided by the\nCommissioner or AFP appointee.\nDishonesty\n(3) For the purposes of this section, dishonest means:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if the person dishonestly represents\nthat a police award has been conferred on the person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\nPolice award\n(2) For the purposes of this section, a police award is an award,\ncommendation, citation, medal or other decoration (however\ndescribed) that has been or may be conferred on the Commissioner\nor an AFP appointee for police services that are provided by the\nCommissioner or AFP appointee.\nDishonesty\n(3) For the purposes of this section, dishonest means:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-62-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-62-ss-2"
