    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-63a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63A Personation etc. of protective service officer or special",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-63a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.186",
      "values:originalText": "protective service officer\n(1) A person, not being a protective service officer or a special\nprotective service officer, must not:\n(a) wear or display any uniform or badge of a protective service\nofficer or special protective service officer, any colourable\nimitation of such a uniform or badge, or any uniform or\nbadge so closely resembling such a uniform or badge as to be\nlikely to deceive; or\n(b) have in the person’s possession any arms or ammunition, or\nany article of clothing, accoutrements or equipment, supplied\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part VI\n\nSection 63B\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nto any protective service officer or special protective service\nofficer.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nThe defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2). See subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "protective service officer\n(1) A person, not being a protective service officer or a special\nprotective service officer, must not:\n(a) wear or display any uniform or badge of a protective service\nofficer or special protective service officer, any colourable\nimitation of such a uniform or badge, or any uniform or\nbadge so closely resembling such a uniform or badge as to be\nlikely to deceive; or\n(b) have in the person’s possession any arms or ammunition, or\nany article of clothing, accoutrements or equipment, supplied\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part VI\n\nSection 63B\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nto any protective service officer or special protective service\nofficer.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nThe defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2). See subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-63a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-63a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9227ba757fc5988de8d1d30a048c1ee21a35f64f74df9717d8586acf654ed2e3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-63a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63A Personation etc. of protective service officer or special",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 186,
      "values:originalText": "protective service officer\n(1) A person, not being a protective service officer or a special\nprotective service officer, must not:\n(a) wear or display any uniform or badge of a protective service\nofficer or special protective service officer, any colourable\nimitation of such a uniform or badge, or any uniform or\nbadge so closely resembling such a uniform or badge as to be\nlikely to deceive; or\n(b) have in the person’s possession any arms or ammunition, or\nany article of clothing, accoutrements or equipment, supplied\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part VI\n\nSection 63B\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979\nCompilation date: 08/11/2025\nto any protective service officer or special protective service\nofficer.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nThe defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2). See subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code."
    },
