    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64AA Suspended AFP employees who are members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-64aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.189",
      "values:originalText": "If an AFP employee who is a member is suspended from duties\nunder the regulations, the member must not, while the suspension\nis in force, exercise any power conferred on a member by this Act\nor any other law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n64AAB  Suspended AFP employees who are protective service\nofficers\nIf an AFP employee who is a protective service officer is\nsuspended from duties under the regulations, the protective service\nofficer must not, while the suspension is in force, exercise any\npower conferred on a protective service officer by this Act or any\nother law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.",
      "skos:definition": "If an AFP employee who is a member is suspended from duties\nunder the regulations, the member must not, while the suspension\nis in force, exercise any power conferred on a member by this Act\nor any other law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n64AAB  Suspended AFP employees who are protective service\nofficers\nIf an AFP employee who is a protective service officer is\nsuspended from duties under the regulations, the protective service\nofficer must not, while the suspension is in force, exercise any\npower conferred on a protective service officer by this Act or any\nother law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64aa-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64aa-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e4e3fcb451891025f78d70f502a5f51fb0e3cc0e7790d558318927a9ca462cce",
      "skos:note": "Member of AFP cannot exercise power while suspended."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-64aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "64AA Suspended AFP employees who are members",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 189,
      "values:originalText": "If an AFP employee who is a member is suspended from duties\nunder the regulations, the member must not, while the suspension\nis in force, exercise any power conferred on a member by this Act\nor any other law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n64AAB  Suspended AFP employees who are protective service\nofficers\nIf an AFP employee who is a protective service officer is\nsuspended from duties under the regulations, the protective service\nofficer must not, while the suspension is in force, exercise any\npower conferred on a protective service officer by this Act or any\nother law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64aa-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64aa"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64aa-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Cannot",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition on exercising power",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64B Liability for wrongful acts of members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-64b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.189",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commonwealth is liable in respect of a tort committed by a\nmember or a protective service officer in the performance or\npurported performance of his or her duties as such a member or a\nprotective service officer in like manner as a person is liable in\nrespect of a tort committed by his or her employee in the course of\nhis or her employment, and shall, in respect of such a tort, be\ntreated for all purposes as a joint tortfeasor with the member or the\nprotective service officer.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commonwealth is liable in respect of a tort committed by a\nmember or a protective service officer in the performance or\npurported performance of his or her duties as such a member or a\nprotective service officer in like manner as a person is liable in\nrespect of a tort committed by his or her employee in the course of\nhis or her employment, and shall, in respect of such a tort, be\ntreated for all purposes as a joint tortfeasor with the member or the\nprotective service officer.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "38e49ea55fbab7b4d27379ee83d617d4d8416d6fc6b78b600efdd67bcbee075e",
      "skos:note": "Liability for wrongful acts of members"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-64b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "64B Liability for wrongful acts of members",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 189,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commonwealth is liable in respect of a tort committed by a\nmember or a protective service officer in the performance or\npurported performance of his or her duties as such a member or a\nprotective service officer in like manner as a person is liable in\nrespect of a tort committed by his or her employee in the course of\nhis or her employment, and shall, in respect of such a tort, be\ntreated for all purposes as a joint tortfeasor with the member or the\nprotective service officer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64b"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64b-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "liability",
      "cml:logicSummary": "State is liable for torts committed by employees",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "66 Protection of persons in respect of work reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-66"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.191",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An action or proceeding, civil or criminal, does not lie against a\nperson in respect of any oral or written report made in good faith\nby the person for the purposes of this Act or the regulations, being\na report about work done, or proposed to be done, by the\nCommissioner, a Deputy Commissioner, an AFP employee, a\nspecial member or a special protective service officer.\n(2) A report is to be taken to have been made in good faith if the\nperson who made it was not actuated by ill will to the\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioner, AFP employee, special\nmember or special protective service officer, as the case may be, or\nby any other improper motive.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply unless:\n(a) the person who made the report believed on reasonable\ngrounds that it was the function or duty of the person to\nwhom the report was made to receive it; and\n(b) if the report contained matter that was false or misleading in\na material respect—the person who made the report did not\nknow, and could not with reasonable diligence have\ndiscovered, that the report contained such matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An action or proceeding, civil or criminal, does not lie against a\nperson in respect of any oral or written report made in good faith\nby the person for the purposes of this Act or the regulations, being\na report about work done, or proposed to be done, by the\nCommissioner, a Deputy Commissioner, an AFP employee, a\nspecial member or a special protective service officer.\n(2) A report is to be taken to have been made in good faith if the\nperson who made it was not actuated by ill will to the\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioner, AFP employee, special\nmember or special protective service officer, as the case may be, or\nby any other improper motive.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply unless:\n(a) the person who made the report believed on reasonable\ngrounds that it was the function or duty of the person to\nwhom the report was made to receive it; and\n(b) if the report contained matter that was false or misleading in\na material respect—the person who made the report did not\nknow, and could not with reasonable diligence have\ndiscovered, that the report contained such matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "059c1ad00c306c5ff120b1dfbef080630795ea9eaf3de720dc206afb469ff6a1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-66",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "66 Protection of persons in respect of work reports",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 191,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An action or proceeding, civil or criminal, does not lie against a\nperson in respect of any oral or written report made in good faith\nby the person for the purposes of this Act or the regulations, being\na report about work done, or proposed to be done, by the\nCommissioner, a Deputy Commissioner, an AFP employee, a\nspecial member or a special protective service officer.\n(2) A report is to be taken to have been made in good faith if the\nperson who made it was not actuated by ill will to the\nCommissioner, Deputy Commissioner, AFP employee, special\nmember or special protective service officer, as the case may be, or\nby any other improper motive.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply unless:\n(a) the person who made the report believed on reasonable\ngrounds that it was the function or duty of the person to\nwhom the report was made to receive it; and\n(b) if the report contained matter that was false or misleading in\na material respect—the person who made the report did not\nknow, and could not with reasonable diligence have\ndiscovered, that the report contained such matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "66(1) Protection of persons in respect of work reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-66-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.191",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An action or proceeding, civil or criminal, does not lie against a\nperson in respect of any oral or written report made in good faith\nby the person for the purposes of this Act or the regulations, being\na report about work done, or proposed to be done, by the\nCommissioner, a Deputy Commissioner, an AFP employee, a\nspecial member or a special protective service officer.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An action or proceeding, civil or criminal, does not lie against a\nperson in respect of any oral or written report made in good faith\nby the person for the purposes of this Act or the regulations, being\na report about work done, or proposed to be done, by the\nCommissioner, a Deputy Commissioner, an AFP employee, a\nspecial member or a special protective service officer.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a53358c5895fb714865781e12ead596503dc26891659f592a24db6407eba89be",
      "skos:note": "Protection from civil or criminal action for reports made in good faith"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-federal-police-act-1979#sec-66-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "66(1) Protection of persons in respect of work reports",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 191,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An action or proceeding, civil or criminal, does not lie against a\nperson in respect of any oral or written report made in good faith\nby the person for the purposes of this Act or the regulations, being\na report about work done, or proposed to be done, by the\nCommissioner, a Deputy Commissioner, an AFP employee, a\nspecial member or a special protective service officer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-66-ss-1-norm",
